window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-07-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-07-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 07 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000072881","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the address that is the same as the one given below.<br><br>C-12, Ashok Vihar,New Delhi,Delhi - 110052 [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"नीचे दिए गए पते के समान पता चुनिए।<br><br>C-12, Ashok Vihar,New Delhi,Delhi - 110052 [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"C-12, Ashok Vihar, New Delhi, Delhi - 110052"},"2":{"en":"C-12, Ashok Vihar, New Delhi, Delhi - 110051"},"3":{"en":"C-12, Ashok Vihar, New Delhi, Delhi - 111052"},"4":{"en":"C-12, Ashok Vihar, New Delhi, Delhi - 110002"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Compare the given address with each option, part by part: house number C-12, locality Ashok Vihar, city New Delhi, state Delhi and PIN 110052.<br>Option (2) writes the PIN as 110051, option (3) as 111052 and option (4) as 110002 — every one of these changes the PIN.<br>Only the first option keeps all the parts, including the PIN 110052, unchanged.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): C-12, Ashok Vihar, New Delhi, Delhi - 110052.</b>","hi":"दिए गए पते की प्रत्येक विकल्प से भाग-दर-भाग तुलना कीजिए: मकान संख्या C-12, इलाका Ashok Vihar, शहर New Delhi, राज्य Delhi तथा पिन 110052।<br>विकल्प (2) में पिन 110051, विकल्प (3) में 111052 तथा विकल्प (4) में 110002 है — इनमें से प्रत्येक पिन बदल देता है।<br>केवल पहले विकल्प में सभी भाग, पिन 110052 सहित, अपरिवर्तित हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): C-12, Ashok Vihar, New Delhi, Delhi - 110052 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000072882","section":"REASONING","topic":"Clock & Calendar","question":{"en":"The seminar in Nagpur happened 1 day before Bhopal. Raipur's seminar was 2 days after Nagpur, and Jabalpur had its seminar 1 day before Raipur. If Bhopal's seminar was on 15<sup>th</sup> July, when was Jabalpur's? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"नागपुर में सेमिनार भोपाल से 1 दिन पहले हुआ। रायपुर का सेमिनार नागपुर के 2 दिन बाद था और जबलपुर का सेमिनार रायपुर से 1 दिन पहले। यदि भोपाल का सेमिनार 15<sup>वीं</sup> जुलाई को था, तो जबलपुर का सेमिनार कब था? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12<sup>th</sup> July","hi":"12<sup>वीं</sup> जुलाई"},"2":{"en":"13<sup>th</sup> July","hi":"13<sup>वीं</sup> जुलाई"},"3":{"en":"14<sup>th</sup> July","hi":"14<sup>वीं</sup> जुलाई"},"4":{"en":"15<sup>th</sup> July","hi":"15<sup>वीं</sup> जुलाई"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Bhopal = 15<sup>th</sup> July<br>Nagpur is 1 day before Bhopal → Nagpur = 14<sup>th</sup> July<br>Raipur is 2 days after Nagpur → Raipur = 16<sup>th</sup> July<br>Jabalpur is 1 day before Raipur → Jabalpur = 15<sup>th</sup> July<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 15<sup>th</sup> July.</b>","hi":"भोपाल = 15<sup>वीं</sup> जुलाई<br>नागपुर भोपाल से 1 दिन पहले → नागपुर = 14<sup>वीं</sup> जुलाई<br>रायपुर नागपुर के 2 दिन बाद → रायपुर = 16<sup>वीं</sup> जुलाई<br>जबलपुर रायपुर से 1 दिन पहले → जबलपुर = 15<sup>वीं</sup> जुलाई<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 15<sup>वीं</sup> जुलाई है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000072883","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If 12 @ 4 = 3, 18 @ 6 = 3, then 20 @ 5 = ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 12 @ 4 = 3, 18 @ 6 = 3, तो 20 @ 5 = ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4"},"2":{"en":"3"},"3":{"en":"5"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"12 @ 4 = 3 means 12 ÷ 4 = 3, and 18 @ 6 = 3 means 18 ÷ 6 = 3.<br>So @ stands for division.<br>20 @ 5 = 20 ÷ 5 = <b>4</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 4.</b>","hi":"12 @ 4 = 3 का अर्थ 12 ÷ 4 = 3 है तथा 18 @ 6 = 3 का अर्थ 18 ÷ 6 = 3 है।<br>अतः @ भाग को दर्शाता है।<br>20 @ 5 = 20 ÷ 5 = <b>4</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000072884","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Analogy","question":{"en":"If 111 → 1367631, 112 → 1404928, then 113 → ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 111 → 1367631, 112 → 1404928, तो 113 → ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1436812"},"2":{"en":"1445000"},"3":{"en":"1435100"},"4":{"en":"1442897"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Check the given pairs: 111 × 111 × 111 = 1367631 and 112 × 112 × 112 = 1404928.<br>So the number is replaced by its cube.<br>113<sup>3</sup> = 113 × 113 × 113 = 12769 × 113 = <b>1442897</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 1442897.</b>","hi":"दिए गए युग्मों की जाँच कीजिए: 111 × 111 × 111 = 1367631 तथा 112 × 112 × 112 = 1404928।<br>अतः संख्या को उसके घन से बदला जाता है।<br>113<sup>3</sup> = 113 × 113 × 113 = 12769 × 113 = <b>1442897</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 1442897 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000072885","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Analogy","question":{"en":"Consider the following analogy:<br>If (15:225::12:144), then which of the following completes the analogy 18 : ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित सादृश्य पर विचार कीजिए:<br>यदि (15:225::12:144) है, तो निम्नलिखित में से कौन सादृश्य 18 : ? को पूर्ण करता है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"306"},"2":{"en":"324"},"3":{"en":"361"},"4":{"en":"289"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"15 : 225 → 225 = 15 × 15, that is the square of the first number.<br>12 : 144 → 144 = 12 × 12, the same rule.<br>So 18 : ? → 18 × 18 = <b>324</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 324.</b>","hi":"15 : 225 → 225 = 15 × 15, अर्थात् पहली संख्या का वर्ग।<br>12 : 144 → 144 = 12 × 12, वही नियम।<br>अतः 18 : ? → 18 × 18 = <b>324</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 324 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000072886","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A 40-liter mixture contains milk and water in the ratio 7:1. How much water must be added to make the ratio 3:1? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"40 लीटर मिश्रण में दूध और पानी का अनुपात 7:1 है। अनुपात 3:1 बनाने के लिए कितना पानी मिलाना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5 liters","hi":"5 लीटर"},"2":{"en":"6.67 liters","hi":"6.67 लीटर"},"3":{"en":"8 liters","hi":"8 लीटर"},"4":{"en":"10 liters","hi":"10 लीटर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Milk = \\(\\frac{7}{8}\\) × 40 = 35 litres, water = 5 litres.<br>Let x litres of water be added; milk stays 35 litres.<br>\\(\\frac{35}{5 + x} = \\frac{3}{1}\\) → 5 + x = \\(\\frac{35}{3}\\) → x = \\(\\frac{35}{3}\\) − 5 = \\(\\frac{20}{3}\\) = 6.67 litres<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 6.67 liters.</b>","hi":"दूध = \\(\\frac{7}{8}\\) × 40 = 35 लीटर, पानी = 5 लीटर।<br>माना x लीटर पानी मिलाया जाता है; दूध 35 लीटर ही रहेगा।<br>\\(\\frac{35}{5 + x} = \\frac{3}{1}\\) → 5 + x = \\(\\frac{35}{3}\\) → x = \\(\\frac{35}{3}\\) − 5 = \\(\\frac{20}{3}\\) = 6.67 लीटर<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 6.67 लीटर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000072887","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Choose the group in which all numbers belong to the same category: [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह समूह चुनिए जिसमें सभी संख्याएँ एक ही श्रेणी की हैं: [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4, 9, 27, 49"},"2":{"en":"11, 13, 17, 19"},"3":{"en":"8, 27, 64,81"},"4":{"en":"2, 3, 5, 9"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Check each group:<br>4, 9, 27, 49 — squares except 27, so not one category.<br>8, 27, 64,81 — cubes (8, 27, 64) but 81 is not a cube.<br>2, 3, 5, 9 — primes except 9.<br>11, 13, 17, 19 — all four are prime numbers.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 11, 13, 17, 19.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक समूह की जाँच कीजिए:<br>4, 9, 27, 49 — 27 के अतिरिक्त सभी वर्ग हैं, अतः एक श्रेणी नहीं।<br>8, 27, 64,81 — 8, 27, 64 घन हैं, परंतु 81 घन नहीं है।<br>2, 3, 5, 9 — 9 के अतिरिक्त सभी अभाज्य हैं।<br>11, 13, 17, 19 — चारों अभाज्य संख्याएँ हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 11, 13, 17, 19 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000072888","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"<b>Instruction:</b> Identify the judgements that must hold for the statement to be valid, then choose the correct option.<br><b>Statement:</b> The government has announced a massive digitalization program aimed at providing all public services through online platforms to reduce bureaucracy and improve accessibility.<br><b>Judgements:</b><br>1. Digitalization will make public services more efficient, accessible, and transparent, improving citizen satisfaction.<br>2. A rapid shift to digital platforms could exclude those without internet access or digital literacy, disproportionately affecting rural or economically disadvantaged populations. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>निर्देश:</b> वे निर्णय पहचानिए जो कथन को वैध बनाने के लिए आवश्यक हैं, फिर सही विकल्प चुनिए।<br><b>कथन:</b> सरकार ने नौकरशाही कम करने और सुलभता बढ़ाने के लिए सभी सार्वजनिक सेवाएँ ऑनलाइन प्लेटफ़ॉर्म के माध्यम से उपलब्ध कराने हेतु एक विशाल डिजिटलीकरण कार्यक्रम की घोषणा की है।<br><b>निर्णय:</b><br>1. डिजिटलीकरण सार्वजनिक सेवाओं को अधिक कुशल, सुलभ और पारदर्शी बनाएगा, जिससे नागरिकों की संतुष्टि बढ़ेगी।<br>2. डिजिटल प्लेटफ़ॉर्म की ओर तेज़ बदलाव उन लोगों को बाहर कर सकता है जिनके पास इंटरनेट या डिजिटल साक्षरता नहीं है, जिसका असर ग्रामीण और आर्थिक रूप से वंचित वर्गों पर अधिक पड़ेगा। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only judgement 1 follows","hi":"केवल निर्णय 1 निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only judgement 2 follows","hi":"केवल निर्णय 2 निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2 follow","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2 follows","hi":"न तो 1 और न ही 2 निकलता है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The programme is announced with the aim of reducing bureaucracy and improving accessibility, so the government must hold that digitalization makes services efficient and accessible — judgement 1 follows.<br>Judgement 2 is a possible risk of the same move and does not have to hold for the statement to be valid.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only judgement 1 follows.</b>","hi":"कार्यक्रम की घोषणा नौकरशाही कम करने और सुलभता बढ़ाने के उद्देश्य से की गई है, अतः सरकार यह मानती है कि डिजिटलीकरण से सेवाएँ कुशल और सुलभ होंगी — निर्णय 1 निकलता है।<br>निर्णय 2 इसी कदम का एक संभावित जोखिम है और कथन की वैधता के लिए आवश्यक नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निर्णय 1 निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000072889","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Complete the series.<br>D3, F5, H7, J9, ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"श्रृंखला पूर्ण कीजिए।<br>D3, F5, H7, J9, ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"K11"},"2":{"en":"M11"},"3":{"en":"L11"},"4":{"en":"N11"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Letters: D, F, H, J → each letter moves 2 steps forward, so the next letter is L.<br>Numbers: 3, 5, 7, 9 → each number increases by 2, so the next number is 11.<br>Next term = <b>L11</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): L11.</b>","hi":"अक्षर: D, F, H, J → प्रत्येक अक्षर 2 स्थान आगे बढ़ता है, अतः अगला अक्षर L है।<br>संख्याएँ: 3, 5, 7, 9 → प्रत्येक संख्या 2 से बढ़ती है, अतः अगली संख्या 11 है।<br>अगला पद = <b>L11</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): L11 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000072890","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"If ‘LION’ is coded as ‘12-9-15-14, ’ how is ‘BEAR’ coded? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि ‘LION’ को ‘12-9-15-14, ’ कूटबद्ध किया जाता है, तो ‘BEAR’ को कैसे कूटबद्ध किया जाएगा? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-5-1-17"},"2":{"en":"2-5-1-18"},"3":{"en":"3-5-1-18"},"4":{"en":"2-6-1-18"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Each letter is replaced by its alphabet position:<br>L = 12, I = 9, O = 15, N = 14 → 12-9-15-14<br>BEAR: B = 2, E = 5, A = 1, R = 18 → <b>2-5-1-18</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2-5-1-18.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर को उसके वर्णमाला क्रमांक से बदला जाता है:<br>L = 12, I = 9, O = 15, N = 14 → 12-9-15-14<br>BEAR: B = 2, E = 5, A = 1, R = 18 → <b>2-5-1-18</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2-5-1-18 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000072891","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"<b>Instruction:</b> Choose the inference that is clearly supported by the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b> The country's agricultural output has seen a decrease due to erratic weather patterns and a lack of advanced farming techniques, despite efforts to improve irrigation and provide financial subsidies to farmers.<br><b>Inference:</b><br>I. Irrigation and financial subsidies alone are insufficient to address the challenges faced by the agriculture sector.<br>II. The weather patterns have become more unpredictable, directly affecting crop yield.<br>III. The efforts to improve the agriculture sector are likely to succeed in the long term, despite current challenges. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>निर्देश:</b> वह निष्कर्ष चुनिए जो कथन से स्पष्ट रूप से समर्थित है।<br><b>कथन:</b> सिंचाई सुधारने और किसानों को वित्तीय सहायता देने के प्रयासों के बावजूद, अनियमित मौसम तथा उन्नत कृषि तकनीकों की कमी के कारण देश के कृषि उत्पादन में कमी आई है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. कृषि क्षेत्र की चुनौतियों का सामना करने के लिए केवल सिंचाई और वित्तीय सहायता पर्याप्त नहीं हैं।<br>II. मौसम का स्वरूप अधिक अनिश्चित हो गया है, जिसका सीधा असर फसल उत्पादन पर पड़ रहा है।<br>III. वर्तमान चुनौतियों के बावजूद कृषि क्षेत्र को सुधारने के प्रयासों को दीर्घकाल में सफलता मिलने की संभावना है। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"If only I follows","hi":"यदि केवल I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"If only II follows","hi":"यदि केवल II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"If both II and III follow","hi":"यदि II और III दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"If both I and II follow","hi":"यदि I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Output fell even though irrigation was improved and subsidies were given, so these efforts alone are not enough — Inference I follows.<br>The statement says the fall is due to erratic weather patterns, so the weather has become unpredictable and is directly affecting the crop yield — Inference II follows.<br>The statement gives no sign of future success, so Inference III does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): If both I and II follow.</b>","hi":"सिंचाई सुधरने और सहायता मिलने के बावजूद उत्पादन घटा है, अतः केवल ये प्रयास पर्याप्त नहीं हैं — निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।<br>कथन के अनुसार कमी अनियमित मौसम के कारण हुई है, अर्थात् मौसम अनिश्चित हो गया है और उसका सीधा असर फसल उत्पादन पर है — निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।<br>कथन में भविष्य में सफलता का कोई संकेत नहीं है, अतः निष्कर्ष III नहीं निकलता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): यदि I और II दोनों निकलते हैं।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000072892","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What is the next number in the series?<br><br>2, 5, 10, 17, 26, ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"श्रृंखला में अगली संख्या क्या है?<br><br>2, 5, 10, 17, 26, ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"35"},"2":{"en":"36"},"3":{"en":"37"},"4":{"en":"38"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Differences: 5 − 2 = 3, 10 − 5 = 5, 17 − 10 = 7, 26 − 17 = 9<br>The differences are the consecutive odd numbers 3, 5, 7, 9, so the next difference is 11.<br>Next number = 26 + 11 = <b>37</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 37.</b>","hi":"अंतर: 5 − 2 = 3, 10 − 5 = 5, 17 − 10 = 7, 26 − 17 = 9<br>अंतर क्रमागत विषम संख्याएँ 3, 5, 7, 9 हैं, अतः अगला अंतर 11 होगा।<br>अगली संख्या = 26 + 11 = <b>37</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 37 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000072893","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"FACTORY\" is written as \"DYARMPW.\" How will \"HOSPITAL\" be written? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"FACTORY\" को \"DYARMPW.\" लिखा जाता है। \"HOSPITAL\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"FNQMGRYJ"},"2":{"en":"GNROHSZK"},"3":{"en":"FMQNGRYJ"},"4":{"en":"GHRONSZK"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"FACTORY → DYARMPW<br>F − 2 = D, A − 2 = Y, C − 2 = A, T − 2 = R, O − 2 = M, R − 2 = P, Y − 2 = W<br>Every letter moves two steps backward.<br>HOSPITAL: H − 2 = F, O − 2 = M, S − 2 = Q, P − 2 = N, I − 2 = G, T − 2 = R, A − 2 = Y, L − 2 = J → <b>FMQNGRYJ</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): FMQNGRYJ.</b>","hi":"FACTORY → DYARMPW<br>F − 2 = D, A − 2 = Y, C − 2 = A, T − 2 = R, O − 2 = M, R − 2 = P, Y − 2 = W<br>प्रत्येक अक्षर दो स्थान पीछे खिसकता है।<br>HOSPITAL: H − 2 = F, O − 2 = M, S − 2 = Q, P − 2 = N, I − 2 = G, T − 2 = R, A − 2 = Y, L − 2 = J → <b>FMQNGRYJ</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): FMQNGRYJ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000072894","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In this following question, four words have been given, out of which three are alike in some manner and the fourth one is different. Choose odd one out. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"इस प्रश्न में चार शब्द दिए गए हैं, जिनमें से तीन किसी प्रकार एक जैसे हैं और चौथा भिन्न है। भिन्न शब्द चुनिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Cabinet Minister","hi":"कैबिनेट मंत्री"},"2":{"en":"Prime Minister","hi":"प्रधान मंत्री"},"3":{"en":"Chief Minister","hi":"मुख्य मंत्री"},"4":{"en":"Chief Justice","hi":"मुख्य न्यायाधीश"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Cabinet Minister, Prime Minister and Chief Minister are all political posts held by members of a government.<br>Chief Justice is a judicial post and is not part of the government.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Chief Justice.</b>","hi":"कैबिनेट मंत्री, प्रधान मंत्री तथा मुख्य मंत्री — ये सभी सरकार के राजनीतिक पद हैं।<br>मुख्य न्यायाधीश एक न्यायिक पद है और सरकार का अंग नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): मुख्य न्यायाधीश है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000072895","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार अथवा स्तंभ-वार एक निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और तदनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"7"},"3":{"en":"5"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Read each row as a three-digit number:<br>First row: 784 = 28 × 28 = 28<sup>2</sup><br>Second row: 729 = 27 × 27 = 27<sup>2</sup><br>So the third row must be 26<sup>2</sup> = 676.<br>6 ? 6 = 676 gives ? = <b>7</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 7.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पंक्ति को तीन अंकों की संख्या के रूप में पढ़िए:<br>पहली पंक्ति: 784 = 28 × 28 = 28<sup>2</sup><br>दूसरी पंक्ति: 729 = 27 × 27 = 27<sup>2</sup><br>अतः तीसरी पंक्ति 26<sup>2</sup> = 676 होनी चाहिए।<br>6 ? 6 = 676 से ? = <b>7</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 7 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000072896","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"There are six members in the family who include P, Q, R, S, T, and U. There are two couples in the family. From the family, it can be understood that Q is a doctor and the father of T. U is a contractor and grandfather of R. S is a housewife and the grandmother of T. The family includes one doctor, one contractor, one nurse, one housewife, and two students belong to the family. Based on this information, identify which pair is definitely a married couple. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"परिवार में छह सदस्य हैं जिनमें P, Q, R, S, T तथा U शामिल हैं। परिवार में दो दंपती हैं। परिवार से यह समझा जा सकता है कि Q डॉक्टर है तथा T का पिता है। U ठेकेदार है तथा R का दादा है। S गृहिणी है तथा T की दादी है। परिवार में एक डॉक्टर, एक ठेकेदार, एक नर्स, एक गृहिणी तथा दो विद्यार्थी हैं। इस जानकारी के आधार पर पहचानिए कि कौन-सा युग्म निश्चित रूप से विवाहित दंपती है। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"U and S","hi":"U तथा S"},"2":{"en":"Q and R","hi":"Q तथा R"},"3":{"en":"T and U","hi":"T तथा U"},"4":{"en":"P and R","hi":"P तथा R"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"93\" y=\"8\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"146\" y=\"8\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M122 14H144M122 18H144M149 68H171M149 72H171M133 18V50M133 50V62M160 72V104M139 104H181M139 104V116M181 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"107\" y=\"22\">U+</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"22\">S−</text><text x=\"133\" y=\"76\">Q+</text><text x=\"186\" y=\"76\">P−</text><text x=\"139\" y=\"130\">T</text><text x=\"181\" y=\"130\">R</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>U is the grandfather and S the grandmother of Q's children, so U and S are the older couple; Q and P form the second couple.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): U and S.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"93\" y=\"8\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"146\" y=\"8\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M122 14H144M122 18H144M149 68H171M149 72H171M133 18V50M133 50V62M160 72V104M139 104H181M139 104V116M181 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"107\" y=\"22\">U+</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"22\">S−</text><text x=\"133\" y=\"76\">Q+</text><text x=\"186\" y=\"76\">P−</text><text x=\"139\" y=\"130\">T</text><text x=\"181\" y=\"130\">R</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>U, Q की संतानों का दादा तथा S दादी है, अतः U और S वरिष्ठ दंपति हैं; Q और P दूसरा दंपति हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): U तथा S है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000072897","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Examine the following roll number series of a batch. Which entry is inconsistent with the pattern that follows an arithmetic progression with a common difference of 6? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी बैच की निम्नलिखित रोल नंबर श्रृंखला का परीक्षण कीजिए। कौन-सी प्रविष्टि उस पैटर्न से असंगत है जो 6 के सार्व अंतर वाली समांतर श्रेणी का पालन करता है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"441005231"},"2":{"en":"441005237"},"3":{"en":"441005243"},"4":{"en":"441005248"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Check the difference between successive entries:<br>441005237 − 441005231 = 6<br>441005243 − 441005237 = 6<br>441005248 − 441005243 = 5<br>The first three entries differ by 6, so the next entry should be 441005243 + 6 = 441005249.<br>Hence 441005248 breaks the pattern.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 441005248.</b>","hi":"क्रमागत प्रविष्टियों का अंतर जाँचिए:<br>441005237 − 441005231 = 6<br>441005243 − 441005237 = 6<br>441005248 − 441005243 = 5<br>पहली तीन प्रविष्टियों का अंतर 6 है, अतः अगली प्रविष्टि 441005243 + 6 = 441005249 होनी चाहिए।<br>इस प्रकार 441005248 पैटर्न को तोड़ती है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 441005248 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000072898","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"Which word cannot be formed from the letters of the word EDUCATION, using each letter only as many times as it appears in the original word? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"शब्द EDUCATION के अक्षरों से कौन-सा शब्द नहीं बनाया जा सकता, यह ध्यान रखते हुए कि प्रत्येक अक्षर का प्रयोग उतनी ही बार किया जाए जितनी बार वह मूल शब्द में है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ACTION"},"2":{"en":"CAUTION"},"3":{"en":"NOTATION"},"4":{"en":"DONATE"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"EDUCATION has the letters E, D, U, C, A, T, I, O, N — only <b>one</b> N.<br>ACTION = A, C, T, I, O, N ✔<br>CAUTION = C, A, U, T, I, O, N ✔<br>DONATE = D, O, N, A, T, E ✔<br>NOTATION needs N twice, which EDUCATION does not have.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): NOTATION.</b>","hi":"EDUCATION में अक्षर हैं E, D, U, C, A, T, I, O, N — इसमें <b>एक ही</b> N है।<br>ACTION = A, C, T, I, O, N ✔<br>CAUTION = C, A, U, T, I, O, N ✔<br>DONATE = D, O, N, A, T, E ✔<br>NOTATION में N दो बार चाहिए, जो EDUCATION में नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): NOTATION है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000072899","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"Rearrange the letters ‘OCRHNOLOGY’ to form a meaningful word.<br><br>Identify the correct option. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"‘OCRHNOLOGY’ अक्षरों को पुनर्व्यवस्थित करके एक सार्थक शब्द बनाइए।<br><br>सही विकल्प पहचानिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"CHRONOLOGY"},"2":{"en":"ARCHEOLOGY"},"3":{"en":"CHRONICAL"},"4":{"en":"ORNITHOLOGY"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Take stock of the letters: O, C, R, H, N, O, L, O, G, Y — that is O three times, and C, R, H, N, L, G, Y once each.<br>CHRONOLOGY uses exactly these letters: C, H, R, O, N, O, L, O, G, Y.<br>ARCHEOLOGY needs an E and two O's, CHRONICAL needs an I and two C's, and ORNITHOLOGY needs I, T and two O's — none of them can be made.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): CHRONOLOGY.</b>","hi":"अक्षरों की गणना कीजिए: O, C, R, H, N, O, L, O, G, Y — अर्थात् O तीन बार तथा C, R, H, N, L, G, Y एक-एक बार।<br>CHRONOLOGY में ठीक यही अक्षर हैं: C, H, R, O, N, O, L, O, G, Y।<br>ARCHEOLOGY में E तथा दो O चाहिए, CHRONICAL में I तथा दो C चाहिए और ORNITHOLOGY में I, T तथा दो O चाहिए — इनमें से कोई भी नहीं बन सकता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): CHRONOLOGY है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000072900","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option which is exactly similar to: 55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow-226001 [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प को चुनिए जो ठीक इसके समान है: 55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow-226001 [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow-226001"},"2":{"en":"55-E, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow-226001"},"3":{"en":"55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow-226002"},"4":{"en":"55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow 226001"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Compare every part: house number 55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow and the PIN written as 226001 after a hyphen.<br>Option (2) changes the house number to 55-E, option (3) changes the PIN to 226002, and option (4) drops the hyphen before the PIN.<br>Only option (1) reproduces the address exactly.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow-226001.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक भाग की तुलना कीजिए: मकान संख्या 55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow तथा योजक चिह्न के बाद पिन 226001।<br>विकल्प (2) में मकान संख्या 55-E हो जाती है, विकल्प (3) में पिन 226002 हो जाता है और विकल्प (4) में पिन से पहले का योजक चिह्न हट जाता है।<br>केवल विकल्प (1) में पता ठीक वैसा ही है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow-226001 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000072901","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statements carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>1. The Internet has become an integral part of our lives.<br>2. Yet there is ongoing debate over whether the Internet is a boon or a curse.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. It is difficult to imagine life without the Internet.<br>II. The constant debate on the Internet is unnecessary. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथनों को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए और उन्हें सत्य मानिए। फिर उनके नीचे दिए गए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय लीजिए कि कौन-सा/कौन-से निष्कर्ष तार्किक रूप से कथन से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>1. इंटरनेट हमारे जीवन का अभिन्न अंग बन गया है।<br>2. फिर भी इस पर लगातार बहस चल रही है कि इंटरनेट वरदान है या अभिशाप।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. इंटरनेट के बिना जीवन की कल्पना करना कठिन है।<br>II. इंटरनेट पर लगातार चलने वाली बहस अनावश्यक है। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both Conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Statement 1 says the Internet has become an integral part of our lives, so life without it is difficult to imagine — Conclusion I follows.<br>Statement 2 only reports that a debate exists; it does not say the debate is unnecessary, so Conclusion II does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only Conclusion I follows.</b>","hi":"कथन 1 कहता है कि इंटरनेट हमारे जीवन का अभिन्न अंग बन गया है, अतः उसके बिना जीवन की कल्पना कठिन है — निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।<br>कथन 2 केवल यह बताता है कि बहस चल रही है; यह नहीं कहता कि बहस अनावश्यक है, अतः निष्कर्ष II नहीं निकलता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000072902","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The government has adversely affected several top-ranking financial institutions by appointing bureaucrats as their directors rather than domain experts.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. The government should appoint directors of financial institutions based on their expertise in the field of finance.<br>II. The director of a financial institution must possess expertise that matches the financial operations handled by the institution. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए गए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय लीजिए कि कौन-सा/कौन-से निष्कर्ष तार्किक रूप से कथन से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>सरकार ने क्षेत्र-विशेषज्ञों के स्थान पर नौकरशाहों को निदेशक नियुक्त करके कई शीर्ष वित्तीय संस्थानों को नुकसान पहुँचाया है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सरकार को वित्तीय संस्थानों के निदेशक वित्त के क्षेत्र में उनकी विशेषज्ञता के आधार पर नियुक्त करने चाहिए।<br>II. वित्तीय संस्थान के निदेशक के पास ऐसी विशेषज्ञता होनी चाहिए जो संस्थान के वित्तीय कार्यों से मेल खाती हो। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Both Conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The statement shows that appointing non-experts harmed the institutions, so directors should be chosen for their expertise — Conclusion I follows.<br>The same reasoning shows that a director must have expertise matching the institution's financial work — Conclusion II also follows.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Both Conclusions I and II follow.</b>","hi":"कथन दर्शाता है कि गैर-विशेषज्ञों की नियुक्ति से संस्थानों को हानि हुई, अतः निदेशक विशेषज्ञता के आधार पर चुने जाने चाहिए — निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।<br>इसी तर्क से यह भी निकलता है कि निदेशक के पास संस्थान के वित्तीय कार्यों से मेल खाती विशेषज्ञता होनी चाहिए — निष्कर्ष II भी निकलता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000072903","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"<b>Examine the eligibility guidelines set for the government tablet distribution scheme by assessing the applications of Student X and Student Y against the stated criteria. Identify which student meets the selection requirements considering the budget constraint given.</b><br><b>Eligibility:</b> A government scheme: “Free tablet computers are provided to students who score 90%+ in Class 10 AND belong to a family with an income &lt; ₹2L/year.”<br><b>Student X:</b> Scored 92%, family income ₹1.9L/year.<br><b>Student Y:</b> Scored 89%, family income ₹1.5L/year.<br><b>Budget Constraint:</b> The remaining tablets are only enough for 1 student. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>सरकारी टैबलेट वितरण योजना के लिए निर्धारित पात्रता दिशानिर्देशों का परीक्षण कीजिए और छात्र X तथा छात्र Y के आवेदनों को दिए गए मानदंडों पर परखिए। दिए गए बजट प्रतिबंध को ध्यान में रखते हुए पहचानिए कि कौन-सा छात्र चयन की शर्तें पूरी करता है।</b><br><b>पात्रता:</b> एक सरकारी योजना: “निःशुल्क टैबलेट कंप्यूटर ऐसे छात्रों को दिए जाते हैं जिन्होंने कक्षा 10 में 90%+ अंक प्राप्त किए हों AND जिनके परिवार की आय &lt; ₹2L/वर्ष हो।”<br><b>छात्र X:</b> 92% अंक, परिवार की आय ₹1.9L/वर्ष।<br><b>छात्र Y:</b> 89% अंक, परिवार की आय ₹1.5L/वर्ष।<br><b>बजट प्रतिबंध:</b> शेष टैबलेट केवल 1 छात्र के लिए पर्याप्त हैं। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Give to Student X because they met the academic criteria.","hi":"छात्र X को दें क्योंकि उसने शैक्षणिक मानदंड पूरा किया है।"},"2":{"en":"Give to Student Y because they are financially weaker.","hi":"छात्र Y को दें क्योंकि वह आर्थिक रूप से अधिक कमजोर है।"},"3":{"en":"Give to neither, as both do not satisfy all criteria.","hi":"किसी को न दें, क्योंकि दोनों सभी मानदंड पूरे नहीं करते।"},"4":{"en":"Split the cost and provide a cheaper device to both.","hi":"लागत बाँटकर दोनों को सस्ता उपकरण दें।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Student X: 92% (≥ 90%) ✔ and income ₹1.9L (&lt; ₹2L) ✔ — both conditions are met.<br>Student Y: 89% is below 90% ✘, so Y is not eligible even though the income is within the limit.<br>Only one tablet is left, and only Student X qualifies, so it goes to Student X.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Give to Student X because they met the academic criteria.</b>","hi":"छात्र X: 92% (≥ 90%) ✔ तथा आय ₹1.9L (&lt; ₹2L) ✔ — दोनों शर्तें पूरी होती हैं।<br>छात्र Y: 89% अंक 90% से कम हैं ✘, अतः आय सीमा के भीतर होने पर भी Y पात्र नहीं है।<br>केवल एक टैबलेट शेष है और केवल छात्र X पात्रता पूरी करता है, इसलिए वह छात्र X को मिलेगा।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): छात्र X को दें क्योंकि उसने शैक्षणिक मानदंड पूरा किया है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000072904","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question two statements are given and these statements are followed by two conclusions. You have to take the given two statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions and then decide which of the given conclusions logically follows from the two given statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>All pens are laptops.<br>All laptops are computers.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. All pens are computers.<br>II. All laptops are pens. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में दो कथन दिए गए हैं और इन कथनों के बाद दो निष्कर्ष हैं। दिए गए दोनों कथनों को सत्य मानना है, चाहे वे सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न प्रतीत हों। निष्कर्षों को पढ़िए और फिर निर्णय लीजिए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-सा दोनों कथनों से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>सभी पेन लैपटॉप हैं।<br>सभी लैपटॉप कंप्यूटर हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सभी पेन कंप्यूटर हैं।<br>II. सभी लैपटॉप पेन हैं। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Pens lie inside laptops and laptops lie inside computers, so every pen is also a computer — Conclusion I follows.<br>Conclusion II is only the converse of the first statement and need not be true.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only conclusion I follows.</b>","hi":"पेन लैपटॉप के भीतर हैं और लैपटॉप कंप्यूटर के भीतर, अतः प्रत्येक पेन कंप्यूटर भी है — निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।<br>निष्कर्ष II पहले कथन का केवल विपर्यय है और सत्य होना आवश्यक नहीं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000072905","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"The regional education board has mandated a compulsory course on personal investment and debt management for all final-year high school students. Which assumption underlies this mandate? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"क्षेत्रीय शिक्षा बोर्ड ने सभी अंतिम वर्ष के हाई स्कूल छात्रों के लिए व्यक्तिगत निवेश तथा ऋण प्रबंधन पर एक अनिवार्य पाठ्यक्रम लागू किया है। इस अनिवार्यता के पीछे कौन-सी पूर्वधारणा है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Formal education is the only method through which students can acquire reliable financial knowledge.","hi":"औपचारिक शिक्षा ही एकमात्र उपाय है जिससे छात्र विश्वसनीय वित्तीय ज्ञान प्राप्त कर सकते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"High school students possess the necessary mathematical foundation to understand complex market trends.","hi":"हाई स्कूल छात्रों के पास जटिल बाज़ार प्रवृत्तियों को समझने का आवश्यक गणितीय आधार है।"},"3":{"en":"Early exposure to financial management concepts will lead to better economic decision-making in adulthood.","hi":"वित्तीय प्रबंधन की अवधारणाओं से प्रारंभिक परिचय वयस्कता में बेहतर आर्थिक निर्णय लेने में सहायक होगा।"},"4":{"en":"Implementing this course will guarantee that no student will ever face significant financial hardship.","hi":"इस पाठ्यक्रम के लागू होने से यह निश्चित हो जाएगा कि किसी भी छात्र को कभी गंभीर आर्थिक कठिनाई नहीं होगी।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The board makes the course compulsory in the final school year, which makes sense only if learning this early carries over into later life.<br>So the mandate assumes that early exposure to financial management leads to better economic decisions in adulthood.<br>The other options either claim exclusivity, guarantee an outcome, or assume a level of mathematics that the mandate does not require.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Early exposure to financial management concepts will lead to better economic decision-making in adulthood.</b>","hi":"बोर्ड इस पाठ्यक्रम को अंतिम स्कूल वर्ष में अनिवार्य बनाता है, जो तभी तर्कसंगत है जब इतनी कम उम्र में सीखी बात आगे के जीवन में काम आए।<br>अतः अनिवार्यता यह मानती है कि वित्तीय प्रबंधन से प्रारंभिक परिचय वयस्कता में बेहतर आर्थिक निर्णयों की ओर ले जाता है।<br>शेष विकल्प या तो एकमात्र उपाय का दावा करते हैं, या परिणाम की गारंटी देते हैं, या ऐसे गणितीय स्तर की अपेक्षा करते हैं जो अनिवार्यता के लिए आवश्यक नहीं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): वित्तीय प्रबंधन की अवधारणाओं से प्रारंभिक परिचय वयस्कता में बेहतर आर्थिक निर्णय लेने में सहायक होगा।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000072906","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: The Mughal Empire","question":{"en":"The arrival of Babur into the Indian subcontinent led to which of the following developments?<br>1. Introduction of paper currency in the Indian subcontinent.<br>2. Establishment of the Timurid dynasty in the region. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"बाबर के भारतीय उपमहाद्वीप में आगमन से निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विकास हुआ?<br>1. भारतीय उपमहाद्वीप में कागज़ी मुद्रा की शुरुआत।<br>2. इस क्षेत्र में तैमूरी वंश की स्थापना। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 only","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"2 only","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2","hi":"न तो 1 और न ही 2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 2 only</b><br>Babur, a descendant of <b>Timur</b> (father's side) and Genghis Khan (mother's side), founded the <b>Mughal (Timurid) dynasty</b> after the First Battle of Panipat (1526). He did not introduce paper currency. Hence <b><u>2 only</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>First Battle of Panipat (1526)</b> – Babur defeated <b>Ibrahim Lodi</b>.<br>• Babur's autobiography <b>Baburnama (Tuzuk-i-Baburi)</b> was written in <b>Turki</b>.<br>• <b>Muhammad bin Tughlaq</b> introduced <b>token currency</b> of copper/brass.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – केवल 2</b><br>बाबर, पिता की ओर से <b>तैमूर</b> और माता की ओर से चंगेज़ ख़ान का वंशज, पानीपत के प्रथम युद्ध (1526) के बाद <b>मुग़ल (तैमूरी) वंश</b> का संस्थापक बना। उसने कागज़ी मुद्रा शुरू नहीं की। अतः <b><u>केवल 2</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>पानीपत का प्रथम युद्ध (1526)</b> – बाबर ने <b>इब्राहिम लोदी</b> को हराया।<br>• बाबर की आत्मकथा <b>बाबरनामा (तुज़ुक-ए-बाबरी)</b> <b>तुर्की</b> भाषा में लिखी गई।<br>• <b>मुहम्मद बिन तुग़लक</b> ने ताँबे/पीतल की <b>सांकेतिक मुद्रा</b> चलाई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000072907","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: National Parks","question":{"en":"The Neora Valley National Park is situated in which state? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"नेओरा वैली राष्ट्रीय उद्यान किस राज्य में स्थित है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Himachal Pradesh","hi":"हिमाचल प्रदेश"},"2":{"en":"West Bengal","hi":"पश्चिम बंगाल"},"3":{"en":"Sikkim","hi":"सिक्किम"},"4":{"en":"Arunachal Pradesh","hi":"अरुणाचल प्रदेश"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – West Bengal</b><br><b>Neora Valley National Park</b> is in the <b>Kalimpong district</b> of <b><u>West Bengal</u></b>; it was established in <b>1986</b> and is known for the red panda.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Other national parks of West Bengal: <b>Sundarbans, Buxa, Jaldapara, Gorumara, Singalila</b>.<br>• <b>Sundarbans</b> is a UNESCO World Heritage Site (1987).<br>• <b>Singalila NP</b> in Darjeeling is also home to the red panda.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पश्चिम बंगाल</b><br><b>नेओरा वैली राष्ट्रीय उद्यान</b> <b><u>पश्चिम बंगाल</u></b> के <b>कलिम्पोंग ज़िले</b> में है; इसकी स्थापना <b>1986</b> में हुई और यह रेड पांडा के लिए प्रसिद्ध है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पश्चिम बंगाल के अन्य राष्ट्रीय उद्यान: <b>सुंदरबन, बक्सा, जलदापाड़ा, गोरुमारा, सिंगालीला</b>।<br>• <b>सुंदरबन</b> यूनेस्को विश्व धरोहर स्थल (1987) है।<br>• दार्जिलिंग का <b>सिंगालीला राष्ट्रीय उद्यान</b> भी रेड पांडा का आवास है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000072908","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Magnetic Effect of Electric Current","question":{"en":"Which of the following pairs <b>correctly</b> matches the physical quantity with its SI unit? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा युग्म भौतिक राशि का उसके SI मात्रक से <b>सही</b> मिलान करता है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Magnetic flux density – Weber","hi":"चुंबकीय फ्लक्स घनत्व – वेबर"},"2":{"en":"Magnetic flux – Tesla","hi":"चुंबकीय फ्लक्स – टेस्ला"},"3":{"en":"Inductance – Henry","hi":"प्रेरकत्व – हेनरी"},"4":{"en":"Electric charge – Volt","hi":"विद्युत आवेश – वोल्ट"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Inductance – Henry</b><br>The SI unit of <b>inductance</b> is the <b><u>henry (H)</u></b>. Flux density is in tesla, flux in weber and charge in coulomb, so the other pairs are wrong.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• 1 tesla = 1 Wb/m².<br>• <b>Volt</b> is the unit of potential difference; 1 V = 1 J/C.<br>• Henry is named after <b>Joseph Henry</b>; 1 H = 1 Wb/A.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – प्रेरकत्व – हेनरी</b><br><b>प्रेरकत्व (Inductance)</b> का SI मात्रक <b><u>हेनरी (H)</u></b> है। फ्लक्स घनत्व टेस्ला में, फ्लक्स वेबर में और आवेश कूलॉम में मापा जाता है, अतः अन्य युग्म गलत हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 1 टेस्ला = 1 Wb/m²।<br>• <b>वोल्ट</b> विभवांतर का मात्रक है; 1 V = 1 J/C।<br>• हेनरी का नाम <b>जोसेफ हेनरी</b> के नाम पर है; 1 H = 1 Wb/A।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000072909","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Solar System","question":{"en":"Which force causes the Earth to bulge at the equator? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा बल पृथ्वी को भूमध्य रेखा पर उभरा हुआ बनाता है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tidal force","hi":"ज्वारीय बल"},"2":{"en":"Centrifugal force","hi":"अपकेंद्री बल"},"3":{"en":"Gravitational force","hi":"गुरुत्वाकर्षण बल"},"4":{"en":"Magnetic force","hi":"चुंबकीय बल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Centrifugal force</b><br>The Earth's rotation produces <b><u>centrifugal force</u></b>, which is maximum at the equator. It makes the Earth bulge at the equator and flatten at the poles (<b>oblate spheroid / geoid</b>).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Equatorial diameter (~12,756 km) is about <b>43 km</b> more than the polar diameter.<br>• The value of <b>g</b> is minimum at the equator and maximum at the poles.<br>• The Earth rotates from <b>west to east</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अपकेंद्री बल</b><br>पृथ्वी के घूर्णन से <b><u>अपकेंद्री बल (Centrifugal force)</u></b> उत्पन्न होता है, जो भूमध्य रेखा पर अधिकतम होता है। इससे पृथ्वी भूमध्य रेखा पर उभरी और ध्रुवों पर चपटी हो जाती है (<b>लघ्वक्ष गोलाभ / जियॉइड</b>)।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भूमध्यरेखीय व्यास (~12,756 km) ध्रुवीय व्यास से लगभग <b>43 km</b> अधिक है।<br>• <b>g</b> का मान भूमध्य रेखा पर न्यूनतम और ध्रुवों पर अधिकतम होता है।<br>• पृथ्वी <b>पश्चिम से पूर्व</b> घूमती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000072910","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Atmosphere","question":{"en":"Which statement <b>accurately</b> describes the behavior of the ionosphere during solar activity? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सौर गतिविधि के दौरान आयनमंडल के व्यवहार का <b>सटीक</b> वर्णन कौन-सा कथन करता है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ionosphere remains completely shielded from solar plasma.","hi":"आयनमंडल सौर प्लाज़्मा से पूर्णतः सुरक्षित रहता है।"},"2":{"en":"Ionospheric density fluctuates with solar flare events.","hi":"सौर ज्वाला घटनाओं के साथ आयनमंडल का घनत्व बदलता रहता है।"},"3":{"en":"Ultraviolet rays stabilize the ionospheric electron density.","hi":"पराबैंगनी किरणें आयनमंडल के इलेक्ट्रॉन घनत्व को स्थिर करती हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Ionospheric layers expand only during the lunar night.","hi":"आयनमंडल की परतें केवल चंद्र रात्रि में फैलती हैं।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Ionospheric density fluctuates with solar flare events.</b><br>The ionosphere is created by ionisation from solar X-rays and UV rays. During <b>solar flares</b>, extra radiation sharply increases ionisation, so <b><u>ionospheric density fluctuates with solar flare events</u></b>, disturbing radio communication.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The ionosphere extends from about <b>80 km to 400 km</b> (part of the thermosphere).<br>• It <b>reflects radio waves</b> back to Earth, enabling long-distance radio communication.<br>• Auroras (<b>Aurora Borealis/Australis</b>) occur in the ionosphere.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सौर ज्वाला घटनाओं के साथ आयनमंडल का घनत्व बदलता रहता है।</b><br>आयनमंडल सौर X-किरणों और UV किरणों द्वारा आयनन से बनता है। <b>सौर ज्वालाओं (Solar flares)</b> के दौरान अतिरिक्त विकिरण से आयनन तेज़ी से बढ़ता है, अतः <b><u>आयनमंडल का घनत्व सौर ज्वाला घटनाओं के साथ बदलता है</u></b>, जिससे रेडियो संचार बाधित होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• आयनमंडल लगभग <b>80 km से 400 km</b> तक फैला है (तापमंडल का भाग)।<br>• यह <b>रेडियो तरंगों को परावर्तित</b> करके पृथ्वी पर लौटाता है, जिससे लंबी दूरी का रेडियो संचार संभव होता है।<br>• ध्रुवीय ज्योतियाँ (<b>ऑरोरा बोरियालिस/ऑस्ट्रेलिस</b>) आयनमंडल में होती हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000072911","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Which state has rich deposits of bauxite in the Patlands of Lohardaga? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"लोहरदगा के पाटलैंड में किस राज्य में बॉक्साइट के समृद्ध भंडार हैं? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Odisha","hi":"ओडिशा"},"2":{"en":"Chhattisgarh","hi":"छत्तीसगढ़"},"3":{"en":"Jharkhand","hi":"झारखंड"},"4":{"en":"Madhya Pradesh","hi":"मध्य प्रदेश"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Jharkhand</b><br>The <b>Pat lands of Lohardaga</b> are in <b><u>Jharkhand</u></b> and have rich <b>bauxite</b> deposits (NCERT).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Odisha</b> is the largest bauxite producer; <b>Panchpatmali (Koraput)</b> has major deposits.<br>• Bauxite is the ore of <b>aluminium</b>.<br>• Other bauxite areas: <b>Amarkantak plateau, Maikal hills, Bilaspur–Katni</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – झारखंड</b><br><b>लोहरदगा के पाट क्षेत्र</b> <b><u>झारखंड</u></b> में हैं, जहाँ <b>बॉक्साइट</b> के समृद्ध भंडार हैं (NCERT)।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>ओडिशा</b> सबसे बड़ा बॉक्साइट उत्पादक है; <b>पंचपटमाली (कोरापुट)</b> में प्रमुख भंडार हैं।<br>• बॉक्साइट <b>एल्युमीनियम</b> का अयस्क है।<br>• अन्य बॉक्साइट क्षेत्र: <b>अमरकंटक पठार, मैकाल पहाड़ियाँ, बिलासपुर–कटनी</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000072912","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Admiral Dinesh Kumar Tripathi is the ___ Chief of Naval Staff of India in 2024. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एडमिरल दिनेश कुमार त्रिपाठी 2024 में भारत के ___ नौसेना प्रमुख हैं। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"24<sup>th</sup>","hi":"24वें"},"2":{"en":"25<sup>th</sup>","hi":"25वें"},"3":{"en":"26<sup>th</sup>","hi":"26वें"},"4":{"en":"27<sup>th</sup>","hi":"27वें"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 26<sup>th</sup></b><br><b>Admiral Dinesh Kumar Tripathi</b> took over as the <b><u>26<sup>th</sup></u></b> Chief of the Naval Staff on <b>30 April 2024</b>, succeeding Admiral R. Hari Kumar.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• He was succeeded by <b>Admiral Krishna Swaminathan</b> as the 27<sup>th</sup> CNS on <b>31 May 2026</b>.<br>• <b>Admiral R. Hari Kumar</b> was the 25<sup>th</sup> CNS.<br>• Navy Day is celebrated on <b>4 December</b> (Operation Trident, 1971).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 26वें</b><br><b>एडमिरल दिनेश कुमार त्रिपाठी</b> ने <b>30 अप्रैल 2024</b> को एडमिरल आर. हरि कुमार के बाद <b><u>26वें</u></b> नौसेना प्रमुख का पदभार संभाला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>31 मई 2026</b> को <b>एडमिरल कृष्णा स्वामीनाथन</b> 27वें नौसेना प्रमुख बने।<br>• <b>एडमिरल आर. हरि कुमार</b> 25वें नौसेना प्रमुख थे।<br>• नौसेना दिवस <b>4 दिसंबर</b> को मनाया जाता है (ऑपरेशन ट्राइडेंट, 1971)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000072913","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Which of the following top-level bureaucratic positions does T. V. Somanathan hold in the Indian government as of 2026? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"2026 तक टी. वी. सोमनाथन भारत सरकार में निम्नलिखित में से किस शीर्ष नौकरशाही पद पर हैं? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Foreign Secretary of India","hi":"भारत के विदेश सचिव"},"2":{"en":"Home Secretary of India","hi":"भारत के गृह सचिव"},"3":{"en":"Cabinet Secretary of India","hi":"भारत के कैबिनेट सचिव"},"4":{"en":"Finance Secretary of India","hi":"भारत के वित्त सचिव"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Cabinet Secretary of India</b><br><b>T.V. Somanathan</b> took charge as the <b><u>Cabinet Secretary of India</u></b> on <b>30 August 2024</b>, succeeding Rajiv Gauba. He was earlier Finance Secretary.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Cabinet Secretary is the <b>senior-most civil servant</b> and heads the <b>Cabinet Secretariat</b>.<br>• He is ex-officio chairman of the <b>Civil Services Board</b>.<br>• The first Cabinet Secretary was <b>N.R. Pillai</b> (1950).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – भारत के कैबिनेट सचिव</b><br><b>टी.वी. सोमनाथन</b> ने <b>30 अगस्त 2024</b> को राजीव गौबा के बाद <b><u>भारत के कैबिनेट सचिव</u></b> का पदभार संभाला। वे पहले वित्त सचिव थे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कैबिनेट सचिव <b>सबसे वरिष्ठ सिविल सेवक</b> हैं और <b>कैबिनेट सचिवालय</b> के प्रमुख होते हैं।<br>• वे <b>सिविल सेवा बोर्ड</b> के पदेन अध्यक्ष हैं।<br>• पहले कैबिनेट सचिव <b>एन.आर. पिल्लई</b> (1950) थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000072914","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"What is the name of the annual water festival held at the Elankavu Bhagavathy Temple in Kerala? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"केरल के एलंकावु भगवती मंदिर में आयोजित वार्षिक जल उत्सव का नाम क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Thrissur Pooram","hi":"त्रिशूर पूरम"},"2":{"en":"Arattu Mahotsavam","hi":"आराट्टु महोत्सवम"},"3":{"en":"Attuvela Mahotsavam","hi":"आट्टुवेला महोत्सवम"},"4":{"en":"Navaratri Mandapam","hi":"नवरात्रि मंडपम"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Attuvela Mahotsavam</b><br><b><u>Attuvela Mahotsavam</u></b> is the annual water festival of the <b>Elankavu Bhagavathy Temple</b> at Vadayar, Kottayam; illuminated, decorated boats (<b>Attuvela</b>) are taken in procession on the river.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Thrissur Pooram</b> – famous temple festival with caparisoned elephants, at Vadakkunnathan Temple.<br>• <b>Nehru Trophy Boat Race</b> is held on Punnamada Lake, Alappuzha.<br>• <b>Onam</b> is the harvest festival of Kerala.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – आट्टुवेला महोत्सवम</b><br><b><u>आट्टुवेला महोत्सवम</u></b> कोट्टायम के वडयार स्थित <b>एलंकावु भगवती मंदिर</b> का वार्षिक जल उत्सव है; इसमें सजी-धजी, रोशन नौकाओं (<b>आट्टुवेला</b>) की नदी में शोभायात्रा निकलती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>त्रिशूर पूरम</b> – वडक्कुनाथन मंदिर में सजे हाथियों वाला प्रसिद्ध मंदिर उत्सव।<br>• <b>नेहरू ट्रॉफी नौका दौड़</b> पुन्नमडा झील, अलप्पुझा में होती है।<br>• <b>ओणम</b> केरल का फसल उत्सव है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000072915","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Indus Valley Civilization","question":{"en":"What underpins the modern academic consensus regarding the end of the Indus civilization? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सिंधु सभ्यता के अंत के संबंध में आधुनिक अकादमिक सहमति का आधार क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A single catastrophic tectonic event","hi":"एक अकेली विनाशकारी विवर्तनिक घटना"},"2":{"en":"Explanations relying purely on human warfare","hi":"केवल मानव युद्ध पर आधारित व्याख्याएँ"},"3":{"en":"A mixture of natural and human factors","hi":"प्राकृतिक और मानवीय कारकों का मिश्रण"},"4":{"en":"Total certainty regarding river diversion","hi":"नदी मार्ग परिवर्तन के संबंध में पूर्ण निश्चितता"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – A mixture of natural and human factors</b><br>Scholars now agree that the decline was gradual and caused by <b><u>a mixture of natural and human factors</u></b> – climate change, drying of rivers (Ghaggar-Hakra), floods, decline in trade and ecological degradation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Mortimer Wheeler</b>'s theory of an <b>Aryan invasion</b> is no longer accepted.<br>• <b>Floods</b> theory – M.R. Sahni; <b>tectonic/ecological</b> theories – Raikes, Fairservis.<br>• The Harappan civilization was discovered in <b>1921</b> by <b>Daya Ram Sahni</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – प्राकृतिक और मानवीय कारकों का मिश्रण</b><br>विद्वान अब मानते हैं कि पतन धीरे-धीरे हुआ और इसके कारण <b><u>प्राकृतिक और मानवीय कारकों का मिश्रण</u></b> थे – जलवायु परिवर्तन, नदियों (घग्गर-हकरा) का सूखना, बाढ़, व्यापार में गिरावट और पारिस्थितिक क्षरण।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>मॉर्टिमर व्हीलर</b> का <b>आर्य आक्रमण</b> सिद्धांत अब स्वीकार्य नहीं है।<br>• <b>बाढ़</b> सिद्धांत – एम.आर. साहनी; <b>विवर्तनिक/पारिस्थितिक</b> सिद्धांत – रेइक्स, फेयरसर्विस।<br>• हड़प्पा सभ्यता की खोज <b>1921</b> में <b>दयाराम साहनी</b> ने की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000072916","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Government Schemes","question":{"en":"What is the main goal of the PM-PRANAM (PM Programme for Restoration, Awareness Generation, Nourishment and Amelioration of Mother Earth) scheme launched by the Government of India? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत सरकार द्वारा शुरू की गई पीएम-प्रणाम (धरती माता की पुनर्स्थापना, जागरूकता सृजन, पोषण और सुधार हेतु प्रधानमंत्री कार्यक्रम) योजना का मुख्य लक्ष्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Promoting rural arts and music","hi":"ग्रामीण कलाओं और संगीत को बढ़ावा देना"},"2":{"en":"Promoting sustainable fertilizer use","hi":"उर्वरकों के सतत उपयोग को बढ़ावा देना"},"3":{"en":"Providing free legal aid to tribal women","hi":"जनजातीय महिलाओं को निःशुल्क विधिक सहायता देना"},"4":{"en":"Renovating ancient religious monuments","hi":"प्राचीन धार्मिक स्मारकों का जीर्णोद्धार"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Promoting sustainable fertilizer use</b><br><b>PM-PRANAM</b> encourages States to <b><u>reduce the use of chemical fertilisers</u></b> and promote balanced, sustainable use with alternatives like organic and bio-fertilisers.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Announced in the <b>Union Budget 2023–24</b>.<br>• <b>50%</b> of the fertiliser subsidy saved by a State is given back to it as a grant.<br>• Related schemes: <b>Soil Health Card (2015)</b>, <b>Nano Urea</b> by IFFCO.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – उर्वरकों के सतत उपयोग को बढ़ावा देना</b><br><b>पीएम-प्रणाम</b> राज्यों को <b><u>रासायनिक उर्वरकों का उपयोग घटाने</u></b> और जैविक व जैव-उर्वरकों जैसे विकल्पों के साथ संतुलित, सतत उपयोग को बढ़ावा देने के लिए प्रोत्साहित करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>केंद्रीय बजट 2023–24</b> में घोषित।<br>• किसी राज्य द्वारा बचाई गई उर्वरक सब्सिडी का <b>50%</b> उसे अनुदान के रूप में लौटाया जाता है।<br>• संबंधित योजनाएँ: <b>मृदा स्वास्थ्य कार्ड (2015)</b>, IFFCO का <b>नैनो यूरिया</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000072917","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Government Schemes","question":{"en":"What is the total annual financial assistance provided to eligible farmers under the PM-KISAN (Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi) scheme in India? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में पीएम-किसान (प्रधानमंत्री किसान सम्मान निधि) योजना के तहत पात्र किसानों को कुल कितनी वार्षिक वित्तीय सहायता दी जाती है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹4,000 per year","hi":"₹4,000 प्रति वर्ष"},"2":{"en":"₹6,000 per year","hi":"₹6,000 प्रति वर्ष"},"3":{"en":"₹8,000 per year","hi":"₹8,000 प्रति वर्ष"},"4":{"en":"₹10,000 per year","hi":"₹10,000 प्रति वर्ष"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – ₹6,000 per year</b><br>Under <b>PM-KISAN</b>, eligible farmer families get <b><u>₹6,000 per year</u></b> in <b>three equal instalments of ₹2,000</b>, paid directly into their bank accounts (DBT).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Launched on <b>24 February 2019</b> at Gorakhpur; a <b>100% Central Sector Scheme</b>.<br>• Implemented by the <b>Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare</b>.<br>• Income-tax payers and institutional landholders are excluded.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – ₹6,000 प्रति वर्ष</b><br><b>पीएम-किसान</b> के तहत पात्र किसान परिवारों को <b><u>₹6,000 प्रति वर्ष</u></b> <b>₹2,000 की तीन समान किस्तों</b> में सीधे बैंक खातों में (DBT) दिए जाते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>24 फरवरी 2019</b> को गोरखपुर से शुरू; <b>100% केंद्रीय क्षेत्र योजना</b>।<br>• <b>कृषि एवं किसान कल्याण मंत्रालय</b> द्वारा कार्यान्वित।<br>• आयकरदाता और संस्थागत भूमिधारक इससे बाहर हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000072918","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Awards and Honours (Current)","question":{"en":"Who is the author of the poetry collection “Animesha”, which received the Sahitya Akademi Award 2025? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025 प्राप्त कविता संग्रह “अनिमेषा” के लेखक कौन हैं? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Sa. Tamilselvan","hi":"स. तमिलसेल्वन"},"2":{"en":"Nandini Sidha Reddy","hi":"नंदिनी सिद्धा रेड्डी"},"3":{"en":"Pritpal Singh Betab","hi":"प्रीतपाल सिंह बेताब"},"4":{"en":"Girijakumar Baliyar Singh","hi":"गिरिजाकुमार बलियार सिंह"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Nandini Sidha Reddy</b><br><b>\"Animesha\"</b>, a <b>Telugu</b> poetry collection by <b><u>Nandini Sidha Reddy</u></b>, received the <b>Sahitya Akademi Award 2025</b> (announced March 2026).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Sa. Tamilselvan</b> won in <b>Tamil</b> for literary criticism.<br>• Awards were given in <b>24 languages</b>; Hindi – <b>Mamta Kalia</b>, English – <b>Navtej Sarna</b>.<br>• The award carries <b>₹1 lakh</b>, a plaque and a shawl.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – नंदिनी सिद्धा रेड्डी</b><br><b><u>नंदिनी सिद्धा रेड्डी</u></b> के <b>तेलुगु</b> कविता संग्रह <b>\"अनिमेषा\"</b> को <b>साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025</b> (मार्च 2026 में घोषित) मिला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>स. तमिलसेल्वन</b> को <b>तमिल</b> में साहित्यिक आलोचना के लिए पुरस्कार मिला।<br>• पुरस्कार <b>24 भाषाओं</b> में दिए गए; हिंदी – <b>ममता कालिया</b>, अंग्रेज़ी – <b>नवतेज सरना</b>।<br>• पुरस्कार में <b>₹1 लाख</b>, ताम्रपत्र और शॉल दिए जाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000072919","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Awards and Honours (Current)","question":{"en":"Who is the author of the short story collection “Bharkhama”, which received the Sahitya Akademi Award 2025? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025 प्राप्त कहानी संग्रह “भरखमा” के लेखक कौन हैं? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Jitender Kumar Soni","hi":"जितेंद्र कुमार सोनी"},"2":{"en":"Nandini Sidha Reddy","hi":"नंदिनी सिद्धा रेड्डी"},"3":{"en":"Pritpal Singh Betab","hi":"प्रीतपाल सिंह बेताब"},"4":{"en":"Girijakumar Baliyar Singh","hi":"गिरिजाकुमार बलियार सिंह"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Jitender Kumar Soni</b><br>The short story collection <b>\"Bharkhama\"</b> by <b><u>Jitender Kumar Soni</u></b> received the <b>Sahitya Akademi Award 2025</b> in <b>Rajasthani</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Sahitya Akademi Awards 2025 covered <b>8 poetry books, 6 short story collections and 4 novels</b> among 24 books.<br>• Sahitya Akademi was set up on <b>12 March 1954</b>; HQ <b>Rabindra Bhavan, New Delhi</b>.<br>• Rajasthani and English are recognised by the Akademi though not in the Eighth Schedule.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – जितेंद्र कुमार सोनी</b><br><b><u>जितेंद्र कुमार सोनी</u></b> के कहानी संग्रह <b>\"भरखमा\"</b> को <b>राजस्थानी</b> भाषा में <b>साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025</b> मिला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025 में 24 पुस्तकों में <b>8 कविता, 6 कहानी संग्रह और 4 उपन्यास</b> थे।<br>• साहित्य अकादमी की स्थापना <b>12 मार्च 1954</b> को हुई; मुख्यालय <b>रवींद्र भवन, नई दिल्ली</b>।<br>• राजस्थानी और अंग्रेज़ी आठवीं अनुसूची में न होते हुए भी अकादमी द्वारा मान्य हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000072920","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A surgeon performs a risky operation on Z with Z’s valid consent. The surgeon knows death is likely but acts in good faith solely to cure Z, without intending death. Z dies during surgery. Which of the following best reflects the legal principle under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 in India? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक सर्जन Z की वैध सहमति से उस पर जोखिमपूर्ण ऑपरेशन करता है। सर्जन जानता है कि मृत्यु की संभावना है, परंतु मृत्यु का आशय रखे बिना केवल Z को ठीक करने के लिए सद्भावपूर्वक कार्य करता है। ऑपरेशन के दौरान Z की मृत्यु हो जाती है। भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 के तहत निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विधिक सिद्धांत सबसे उपयुक्त है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The surgeon is guilty because knowledge of likely death always creates liability.","hi":"सर्जन दोषी है क्योंकि संभावित मृत्यु का ज्ञान सदैव दायित्व उत्पन्न करता है।"},"2":{"en":"The Surgeon protected as act was in good faith with Z’s consent for Z’s benefit.","hi":"सर्जन संरक्षित है क्योंकि कार्य Z की सहमति से, Z के लाभ के लिए सद्भावपूर्वक किया गया।"},"3":{"en":"The surgeon is protected only if death was impossible to foresee.","hi":"सर्जन तभी संरक्षित है जब मृत्यु का पूर्वानुमान असंभव हो।"},"4":{"en":"Consent is irrelevant where death occurs.","hi":"मृत्यु होने पर सहमति अप्रासंगिक है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – The Surgeon protected as act was in good faith with Z’s consent for Z’s benefit.</b><br><b>Section 26 of the BNS</b> (old IPC Sec. 88) protects an act <b>not intended to cause death</b>, done by consent <b>in good faith for the person's benefit</b>, even if the doer knows it is likely to cause death. So the <b><u>surgeon is protected</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Such provisions fall under <b>\"General Exceptions\"</b> (Chapter III, BNS).<br>• <b>Section 25 BNS</b> – consent for acts not intended or known to cause death/grievous hurt.<br>• BNS replaced the <b>IPC, 1860</b> from <b>1 July 2024</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सर्जन संरक्षित है क्योंकि कार्य Z की सहमति से, Z के लाभ के लिए सद्भावपूर्वक किया गया।</b><br><b>BNS की धारा 26</b> (पुरानी IPC धारा 88) ऐसे कार्य को संरक्षण देती है जो <b>मृत्यु कारित करने के आशय से नहीं</b>, बल्कि <b>व्यक्ति के लाभ के लिए सद्भावपूर्वक</b> सहमति से किया गया हो, भले ही करने वाला जानता हो कि इससे मृत्यु संभव है। अतः <b><u>सर्जन संरक्षित है</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ऐसे प्रावधान <b>\"साधारण अपवाद\"</b> (BNS, अध्याय III) में आते हैं।<br>• <b>BNS धारा 25</b> – मृत्यु/घोर उपहति कारित करने के आशय या ज्ञान से रहित कार्यों के लिए सहमति।<br>• BNS ने <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से <b>IPC, 1860</b> का स्थान लिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000072921","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who became the first woman to be appointed as the Chairperson and Chief Executive Officer (CEO) of the Railway Board in September 2023? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सितंबर 2023 में रेलवे बोर्ड की अध्यक्ष और मुख्य कार्यकारी अधिकारी (CEO) नियुक्त होने वाली पहली महिला कौन बनीं? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Soma Mondal","hi":"सोमा मंडल"},"2":{"en":"Jaya Varma Sinha","hi":"जया वर्मा सिन्हा"},"3":{"en":"Madhabi Puri Buch","hi":"माधबी पुरी बुच"},"4":{"en":"Alka Mittal","hi":"अलका मित्तल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Jaya Varma Sinha</b><br><b><u>Jaya Varma Sinha</u></b> became the first woman <b>Chairperson and CEO of the Railway Board</b> on <b>1 September 2023</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Soma Mondal</b> – first woman Chairman of <b>SAIL</b>.<br>• <b>Madhabi Puri Buch</b> – first woman Chairperson of <b>SEBI</b>.<br>• <b>Alka Mittal</b> – first woman CMD of <b>ONGC</b> (interim).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – जया वर्मा सिन्हा</b><br><b><u>जया वर्मा सिन्हा</u></b> <b>1 सितंबर 2023</b> को <b>रेलवे बोर्ड की अध्यक्ष और CEO</b> बनने वाली पहली महिला बनीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>सोमा मंडल</b> – <b>SAIL</b> की पहली महिला अध्यक्ष।<br>• <b>माधबी पुरी बुच</b> – <b>SEBI</b> की पहली महिला अध्यक्ष।<br>• <b>अलका मित्तल</b> – <b>ONGC</b> की पहली महिला CMD (अंतरिम)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000072922","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who was continued as Principal Secretary to the Prime Minister of India in June 2024? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"जून 2024 में भारत के प्रधानमंत्री के प्रधान सचिव के रूप में किसे बनाए रखा गया? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Nripendra Misra","hi":"नृपेंद्र मिश्रा"},"2":{"en":"P.K. Mishra","hi":"पी.के. मिश्रा"},"3":{"en":"Pramod Kumar Sharma","hi":"प्रमोद कुमार शर्मा"},"4":{"en":"Tarun Bajaj","hi":"तरुण बजाज"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – P.K. Mishra</b><br><b><u>Dr. P.K. Mishra</u></b> was re-appointed as <b>Principal Secretary to the PM</b> in <b>June 2024</b>, co-terminus with the PM's term, after the new government took office.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Ajit Doval</b> was also continued as the <b>National Security Adviser</b> in June 2024.<br>• <b>Shaktikanta Das</b> was appointed <b>Principal Secretary-2</b> to the PM in February 2025.<br>• <b>Nripendra Misra</b> was the first Principal Secretary to PM Modi (2014–2019).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पी.के. मिश्रा</b><br>नई सरकार के गठन के बाद <b>जून 2024</b> में <b><u>डॉ. पी.के. मिश्रा</u></b> को प्रधानमंत्री के कार्यकाल के साथ <b>प्रधानमंत्री के प्रधान सचिव</b> पद पर पुनः नियुक्त किया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• जून 2024 में <b>अजीत डोभाल</b> को भी <b>राष्ट्रीय सुरक्षा सलाहकार</b> पद पर बनाए रखा गया।<br>• फरवरी 2025 में <b>शक्तिकांत दास</b> को प्रधानमंत्री का <b>प्रधान सचिव-2</b> नियुक्त किया गया।<br>• <b>नृपेंद्र मिश्रा</b> प्रधानमंत्री मोदी के पहले प्रधान सचिव (2014–2019) थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000072923","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements regarding Indo-Islamic architecture:<br>1. It is conventionally divided into the Imperial, Provincial, Mughal, and Deccani styles.<br>2. The Provincial style includes the architectural traditions of Gujarat, Bengal, and Jaunpur.<br>Which of the statements given above is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"हिंद-इस्लामी स्थापत्य के संबंध में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>1. इसे परंपरागत रूप से शाही, प्रांतीय, मुग़ल और दक्कनी शैलियों में बाँटा जाता है।<br>2. प्रांतीय शैली में गुजरात, बंगाल और जौनपुर की स्थापत्य परंपराएँ शामिल हैं।<br>ऊपर दिए गए कथनों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 only","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"2 only","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2","hi":"न तो 1 और न ही 2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Both 1 and 2</b><br>Indo-Islamic architecture is classified into <b>Imperial (Delhi Sultanate), Provincial, Mughal and Deccani</b> styles, and the Provincial style covers <b>Gujarat, Bengal, Jaunpur, Malwa</b> etc. Both statements are correct: <b><u>Both 1 and 2</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Jaunpur's <b>Atala Masjid</b> is a fine example of the Sharqi style.<br>• Bengal style used <b>brick and terracotta</b>, e.g., <b>Adina Mosque</b> (Pandua).<br>• Deccani style: <b>Gol Gumbaz (Bijapur), Charminar (Hyderabad)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 1 और 2 दोनों</b><br>हिंद-इस्लामी स्थापत्य को <b>शाही (दिल्ली सल्तनत), प्रांतीय, मुग़ल और दक्कनी</b> शैलियों में बाँटा जाता है, और प्रांतीय शैली में <b>गुजरात, बंगाल, जौनपुर, मालवा</b> आदि शामिल हैं। दोनों कथन सही हैं: <b><u>1 और 2 दोनों</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• जौनपुर की <b>अटाला मस्जिद</b> शर्की शैली का उत्कृष्ट उदाहरण है।<br>• बंगाल शैली में <b>ईंट और टेराकोटा</b> का प्रयोग, जैसे <b>अदीना मस्जिद</b> (पांडुआ)।<br>• दक्कनी शैली: <b>गोल गुंबज़ (बीजापुर), चारमीनार (हैदराबाद)</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000072924","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Which of the following industries continued to remain under industrial licensing even after the economic reforms initiated in 1991? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1991 में शुरू हुए आर्थिक सुधारों के बाद भी निम्नलिखित में से कौन-से उद्योग औद्योगिक लाइसेंसिंग के अंतर्गत बने रहे? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Automobile and textile industries","hi":"ऑटोमोबाइल और वस्त्र उद्योग"},"2":{"en":"Alcohol and hazardous chemicals","hi":"शराब और खतरनाक रसायन"},"3":{"en":"Cement and chemical fertiliser","hi":"सीमेंट और रासायनिक उर्वरक"},"4":{"en":"Sugar and paper manufacturing","hi":"चीनी और कागज़ निर्माण"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Alcohol and hazardous chemicals</b><br>As per NCERT, after 1991 licensing was abolished except for industries like <b><u>alcohol, cigarettes, hazardous chemicals</u></b>, industrial explosives, electronics/aerospace and drugs and pharmaceuticals.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>New Industrial Policy</b> was announced on <b>24 July 1991</b>.<br>• Today compulsory licensing applies to only a few industries such as <b>tobacco products, hazardous chemicals, defence equipment</b>.<br>• Industries reserved for the public sector now: <b>atomic energy and railway operations</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – शराब और खतरनाक रसायन</b><br>NCERT के अनुसार 1991 के बाद <b><u>शराब, सिगरेट, खतरनाक रसायन</u></b>, औद्योगिक विस्फोटक, इलेक्ट्रॉनिक्स/एयरोस्पेस और औषधि जैसे उद्योगों को छोड़कर लाइसेंसिंग समाप्त कर दी गई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>नई औद्योगिक नीति</b> <b>24 जुलाई 1991</b> को घोषित हुई।<br>• आज अनिवार्य लाइसेंसिंग केवल कुछ उद्योगों पर लागू है, जैसे <b>तंबाकू उत्पाद, खतरनाक रसायन, रक्षा उपकरण</b>।<br>• सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र हेतु आरक्षित उद्योग अब: <b>परमाणु ऊर्जा और रेल परिचालन</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000072925","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"The Indian Premier League (IPL) 2025 final, in which Royal Challengers Bengaluru won their maiden title, was played on 3 June 2025 at which of the following venues? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"इंडियन प्रीमियर लीग (IPL) 2025 का फाइनल, जिसमें रॉयल चैलेंजर्स बेंगलुरु ने अपना पहला खिताब जीता, 3 जून 2025 को निम्नलिखित में से किस स्थल पर खेला गया? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Eden Gardens, Kolkata","hi":"ईडन गार्डन्स, कोलकाता"},"2":{"en":"Narendra Modi Stadium, Ahmedabad","hi":"नरेंद्र मोदी स्टेडियम, अहमदाबाद"},"3":{"en":"Wankhede Stadium, Mumbai","hi":"वानखेड़े स्टेडियम, मुंबई"},"4":{"en":"Muthiah Annamalai Chidambaram Stadium, Chennai","hi":"मुथैया अन्नामलाई चिदंबरम स्टेडियम, चेन्नई"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Narendra Modi Stadium, Ahmedabad</b><br>The <b>IPL 2025 final</b> was played at the <b><u>Narendra Modi Stadium, Ahmedabad</u></b>, where <b>RCB</b> beat <b>Punjab Kings</b> by 6 runs to win their first title.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• RCB was captained by <b>Rajat Patidar</b>; <b>Krunal Pandya</b> was Player of the Match in the final.<br>• Orange Cap: <b>Sai Sudharsan</b> (GT); Purple Cap: <b>Prasidh Krishna</b> (GT).<br>• IPL began in <b>2008</b>; Mumbai Indians and CSK have won 5 titles each.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – नरेंद्र मोदी स्टेडियम, अहमदाबाद</b><br><b>IPL 2025 फाइनल</b> <b><u>नरेंद्र मोदी स्टेडियम, अहमदाबाद</u></b> में खेला गया, जहाँ <b>RCB</b> ने <b>पंजाब किंग्स</b> को 6 रन से हराकर पहला खिताब जीता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• RCB के कप्तान <b>रजत पाटीदार</b> थे; फाइनल में <b>क्रुणाल पांड्या</b> प्लेयर ऑफ द मैच रहे।<br>• ऑरेंज कैप: <b>साई सुदर्शन</b> (GT); पर्पल कैप: <b>प्रसिद्ध कृष्णा</b> (GT)।<br>• IPL <b>2008</b> में शुरू हुआ; मुंबई इंडियंस और CSK ने 5-5 खिताब जीते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000072926","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"Adult literacy rate was replaced in Human Development Index (HDI) methodology mainly because: [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मानव विकास सूचकांक (HDI) की कार्यप्रणाली में वयस्क साक्षरता दर को मुख्य रूप से क्यों बदला गया? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It did not receive adequate acceptance from most countries.","hi":"इसे अधिकांश देशों से पर्याप्त स्वीकृति नहीं मिली।"},"2":{"en":"It did not adequately reflect the education dimension.","hi":"यह शिक्षा आयाम को पर्याप्त रूप से नहीं दर्शाती थी।"},"3":{"en":"It did not adequately capture differences in educational attainment.","hi":"यह शैक्षिक उपलब्धि में अंतर को पर्याप्त रूप से नहीं दर्शाती थी।"},"4":{"en":"It did not provide reliable calculations for developing countries.","hi":"यह विकासशील देशों के लिए विश्वसनीय गणना नहीं देती थी।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – It did not adequately capture differences in educational attainment.</b><br>Adult literacy only shows whether a person can read and write; it <b><u>does not capture differences in educational attainment</u></b>. So in <b>2010</b> UNDP replaced it with <b>mean years of schooling</b> and <b>expected years of schooling</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In 2010, <b>GDP per capita</b> was also replaced by <b>GNI per capita</b>.<br>• HDI is calculated as the <b>geometric mean</b> of the three indices (since 2010).<br>• HDI was first published in <b>1990</b> by UNDP.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – यह शैक्षिक उपलब्धि में अंतर को पर्याप्त रूप से नहीं दर्शाती थी।</b><br>वयस्क साक्षरता केवल यह दर्शाती है कि व्यक्ति पढ़-लिख सकता है या नहीं; यह <b><u>शैक्षिक उपलब्धि के अंतर को नहीं दर्शाती</u></b>। इसलिए <b>2010</b> में UNDP ने इसे <b>स्कूली शिक्षा के औसत वर्ष</b> और <b>अपेक्षित वर्ष</b> से बदल दिया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 2010 में <b>प्रति व्यक्ति GDP</b> को भी <b>प्रति व्यक्ति GNI</b> से बदला गया।<br>• HDI तीनों सूचकांकों के <b>गुणोत्तर माध्य</b> के रूप में (2010 से) गणना होता है।<br>• HDI पहली बार <b>1990</b> में UNDP ने प्रकाशित किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000072927","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which government department coordinates the Business Reforms Action Plan (BRAP) exercise in India? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में व्यापार सुधार कार्य योजना (BRAP) प्रक्रिया का समन्वय कौन-सा सरकारी विभाग करता है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade","hi":"उद्योग और आंतरिक व्यापार संवर्धन विभाग"},"2":{"en":"Department for National Planning and Institutional Transformation","hi":"राष्ट्रीय नियोजन और संस्थागत परिवर्तन विभाग"},"3":{"en":"Department for Securities Regulation and Investor Protection","hi":"प्रतिभूति विनियमन और निवेशक संरक्षण विभाग"},"4":{"en":"Department for Banking Regulation and Monetary Policy","hi":"बैंकिंग विनियमन और मौद्रिक नीति विभाग"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade</b><br>The <b>Business Reforms Action Plan (BRAP)</b> is coordinated by the <b><u>Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade (DPIIT)</u></b>, Ministry of Commerce and Industry, to rank States on ease of doing business.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• BRAP was started in <b>2014</b>.<br>• DPIIT was renamed from <b>DIPP</b> in <b>2019</b>.<br>• DPIIT also handles <b>Startup India</b> and FDI policy.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – उद्योग और आंतरिक व्यापार संवर्धन विभाग</b><br><b>व्यापार सुधार कार्य योजना (BRAP)</b> का समन्वय वाणिज्य और उद्योग मंत्रालय का <b><u>उद्योग और आंतरिक व्यापार संवर्धन विभाग (DPIIT)</u></b> करता है, जो व्यापार सुगमता पर राज्यों को रैंक करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BRAP <b>2014</b> में शुरू हुआ।<br>• <b>DIPP</b> का नाम बदलकर <b>2019</b> में DPIIT किया गया।<br>• DPIIT <b>स्टार्टअप इंडिया</b> और FDI नीति का भी कार्य देखता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000072928","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"What is the primary objective of the Central Inspection System under the Business Reforms Action Plan? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"व्यापार सुधार कार्य योजना के अंतर्गत केंद्रीय निरीक्षण प्रणाली का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Introduce inspection free regulatory procedures","hi":"निरीक्षण-मुक्त विनियामक प्रक्रियाएँ लागू करना"},"2":{"en":"Introduce privately managed inspection procedures","hi":"निजी रूप से प्रबंधित निरीक्षण प्रक्रियाएँ लागू करना"},"3":{"en":"Introduce more frequent inspection procedures","hi":"अधिक बार होने वाली निरीक्षण प्रक्रियाएँ लागू करना"},"4":{"en":"Introduce integrated risk based inspections","hi":"एकीकृत जोखिम-आधारित निरीक्षण लागू करना"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Introduce integrated risk based inspections</b><br>The <b>Central Inspection System</b> aims to introduce <b><u>integrated, risk-based inspections</u></b> – joint, computer-allocated inspections based on the risk level of units – to reduce harassment and the burden on businesses.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Inspection reports are to be uploaded online within <b>48 hours</b>.<br>• Low-risk units may be allowed <b>self-certification / third-party certification</b>.<br>• It is part of improving the <b>Ease of Doing Business</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – एकीकृत जोखिम-आधारित निरीक्षण लागू करना</b><br><b>केंद्रीय निरीक्षण प्रणाली</b> का उद्देश्य <b><u>एकीकृत, जोखिम-आधारित निरीक्षण</u></b> लागू करना है – इकाइयों के जोखिम स्तर पर आधारित संयुक्त, कंप्यूटर द्वारा आवंटित निरीक्षण – जिससे व्यवसायों पर बोझ और उत्पीड़न कम हो।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• निरीक्षण रिपोर्टें <b>48 घंटे</b> के भीतर ऑनलाइन अपलोड करनी होती हैं।<br>• कम जोखिम वाली इकाइयों को <b>स्व-प्रमाणन / तृतीय-पक्ष प्रमाणन</b> की अनुमति हो सकती है।<br>• यह <b>व्यापार सुगमता</b> सुधारने का भाग है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000072929","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"Why are pollinators such as insects, birds, and bats considered ecologically important? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कीट, पक्षी और चमगादड़ जैसे परागणकर्ताओं को पारिस्थितिक रूप से महत्वपूर्ण क्यों माना जाता है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They are more economically valuable than entire forest ecosystems.","hi":"वे संपूर्ण वन पारितंत्रों से अधिक आर्थिक रूप से मूल्यवान हैं।"},"2":{"en":"They demonstrate the ecological interdependence between forests and agriculture.","hi":"वे वनों और कृषि के बीच पारिस्थितिक परस्पर निर्भरता को दर्शाते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"They are the primary species threatened by tourism.","hi":"वे पर्यटन से खतरे में आने वाली प्रमुख प्रजातियाँ हैं।"},"4":{"en":"They directly support industrial manufacturing processes.","hi":"वे सीधे औद्योगिक विनिर्माण प्रक्रियाओं में सहायता करते हैं।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – They demonstrate the ecological interdependence between forests and agriculture.</b><br>Pollinators living in forests and natural habitats pollinate crops on nearby farms, so they show the <b><u>ecological interdependence between forests and agriculture</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• About <b>75%</b> of food crops depend at least partly on animal pollination.<br>• <b>Bees</b> are the most important pollinators; <b>bats</b> pollinate night-blooming plants.<br>• <b>World Bee Day</b> is observed on <b>20 May</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – वे वनों और कृषि के बीच पारिस्थितिक परस्पर निर्भरता को दर्शाते हैं।</b><br>वनों और प्राकृतिक आवासों में रहने वाले परागणकर्ता निकटवर्ती खेतों की फसलों का परागण करते हैं, अतः वे <b><u>वनों और कृषि के बीच पारिस्थितिक परस्पर निर्भरता</u></b> दर्शाते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• लगभग <b>75%</b> खाद्य फसलें कम से कम आंशिक रूप से जंतु परागण पर निर्भर हैं।<br>• <b>मधुमक्खियाँ</b> सबसे महत्वपूर्ण परागणकर्ता हैं; <b>चमगादड़</b> रात में खिलने वाले पौधों का परागण करते हैं।<br>• <b>विश्व मधुमक्खी दिवस</b> <b>20 मई</b> को मनाया जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000072930","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Basics of Economy","question":{"en":"Why does the fundamental economic problem of scarcity arise? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"अभाव (scarcity) की मूलभूत आर्थिक समस्या क्यों उत्पन्न होती है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Because governments intentionally limit all production","hi":"क्योंकि सरकारें जानबूझकर सारे उत्पादन को सीमित करती हैं"},"2":{"en":"Because wants exceed available resources","hi":"क्योंकि आवश्यकताएँ उपलब्ध संसाधनों से अधिक हैं"},"3":{"en":"Because firms always attempt to maximise profits","hi":"क्योंकि फर्में सदैव लाभ को अधिकतम करने का प्रयास करती हैं"},"4":{"en":"Because the prices of all goods remain high","hi":"क्योंकि सभी वस्तुओं की कीमतें ऊँची रहती हैं"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Because wants exceed available resources</b><br>Scarcity arises because human <b>wants are unlimited</b> while <b>resources are limited</b> and have alternative uses – i.e., <b><u>wants exceed available resources</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Scarcity leads to the problem of <b>choice</b> and the concept of <b>opportunity cost</b>.<br>• Central problems of an economy: <b>what to produce, how to produce, for whom to produce</b>.<br>• <b>Lionel Robbins</b> defined economics as a science of scarcity and choice.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – क्योंकि आवश्यकताएँ उपलब्ध संसाधनों से अधिक हैं</b><br>अभाव इसलिए उत्पन्न होता है क्योंकि मानव <b>आवश्यकताएँ असीमित</b> हैं जबकि <b>संसाधन सीमित</b> हैं और उनके वैकल्पिक उपयोग हैं – अर्थात् <b><u>आवश्यकताएँ उपलब्ध संसाधनों से अधिक हैं</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अभाव से <b>चयन</b> की समस्या और <b>अवसर लागत</b> की अवधारणा उत्पन्न होती है।<br>• अर्थव्यवस्था की केंद्रीय समस्याएँ: <b>क्या उत्पादन करें, कैसे करें, किसके लिए करें</b>।<br>• <b>लियोनेल रॉबिंस</b> ने अर्थशास्त्र को अभाव और चयन का विज्ञान बताया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000072931","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In a polygon, the largest angle is 12° more than the average of all its interior angles. If the largest angle measures 4/3 of a right angle, find the number of sides of the polygon. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक बहुभुज में सबसे बड़ा कोण उसके सभी अंतःकोणों के औसत से 12° अधिक है। यदि सबसे बड़ा कोण एक समकोण का 4/3 है, तो बहुभुज की भुजाओं की संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8"},"2":{"en":"7"},"3":{"en":"6"},"4":{"en":"5"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Largest angle \\(= \\frac{4}{3} \\times 90° = 120°\\)<br>Average angle \\(= 120° - 12° = 108°\\)<br>\\(\\frac{(n - 2)180°}{n} = 108° \\Rightarrow 180n - 360 = 108n \\Rightarrow 72n = 360\\)<br>\\(n = \\boxed{5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 5.</b>","hi":"सबसे बड़ा कोण \\(= \\frac{4}{3} \\times 90° = 120°\\)<br>औसत कोण \\(= 120° - 12° = 108°\\)<br>\\(\\frac{(n - 2)180°}{n} = 108° \\Rightarrow 180n - 360 = 108n \\Rightarrow 72n = 360\\)<br>\\(n = \\boxed{5}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000072932","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"What is the inradius of an equilateral triangle with a side length of 6 cm? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"6 cm भुजा वाले समबाहु त्रिभुज की अंतःत्रिज्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1.11 cm"},"2":{"en":"1.73 cm"},"3":{"en":"3.37 cm"},"4":{"en":"2.21 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"248\" height=\"232\" viewBox=\"0 0 248 232\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M124 26L26 196L222 196ZM124 139L124 196M130 196L130 190L124 190\"/><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"139\" r=\"57\"/><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"139\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"124\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"207\">B</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"207\">C</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"139\">I</text><text x=\"128\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">r</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"11\">6 cm</text></g></svg><br>\\(r = \\frac{a}{2\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br>\\(r = \\sqrt{3} = 1.732\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1.73\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1.73 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"248\" height=\"232\" viewBox=\"0 0 248 232\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M124 26L26 196L222 196ZM124 139L124 196M130 196L130 190L124 190\"/><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"139\" r=\"57\"/><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"139\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"124\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"207\">B</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"207\">C</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"139\">I</text><text x=\"128\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">r</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"11\">6 cm</text></g></svg><br>\\(r = \\frac{a}{2\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br>\\(r = \\sqrt{3} = 1.732\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1.73\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1.73 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000072933","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"Find the value of k, if x = 1, y = 2 is a solution of the equation 2x + 3y = k. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"k का मान ज्ञात कीजिए, यदि x = 1, y = 2 समीकरण 2x + 3y = k का हल है। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"-8"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"6"},"4":{"en":"8"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Substitute \\(x = 1\\), \\(y = 2\\)<br>\\(k = 2(1) + 3(2) = 2 + 6\\)<br>\\(k = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 8.</b>","hi":"\\(x = 1\\), \\(y = 2\\) रखिए<br>\\(k = 2(1) + 3(2) = 2 + 6\\)<br>\\(k = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000072934","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"If two lines are perpendicular and one has a slope of a/b, what is the slope of the other? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि दो रेखाएँ लंबवत हैं और एक की प्रवणता a/b है, तो दूसरी की प्रवणता क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"-b/a"},"2":{"en":"-a/b"},"3":{"en":"0"},"4":{"en":"1"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"For perpendicular lines, \\(m_1 m_2 = -1\\)<br>\\(m_2 = -\\frac{1}{a/b} = \\boxed{-\\frac{b}{a}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): -b/a.</b>","hi":"लंबवत रेखाओं के लिए \\(m_1 m_2 = -1\\)<br>\\(m_2 = -\\frac{1}{a/b} = \\boxed{-\\frac{b}{a}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): -b/a है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000072935","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If θ = 2π/3 radians, find the quadrant in which θ lies. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि θ = 2π/3 रेडियन है, तो θ किस चतुर्थांश में स्थित है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"I"},"2":{"en":"II"},"3":{"en":"III"},"4":{"en":"IV"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\theta = \\frac{2\\pi}{3} = 120°\\)<br>\\(90° < 120° < 180°\\)<br>So θ lies in quadrant \\(\\boxed{II}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): II.</b>","hi":"\\(\\theta = \\frac{2\\pi}{3} = 120°\\)<br>\\(90° < 120° < 180°\\)<br>अतः θ \\(\\boxed{II}\\) चतुर्थांश में है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): II है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000072936","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"Determine the number to be added to 144p² − 72p so that it becomes a perfect square. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"144p² − 72p में कौन-सी संख्या जोड़ी जाए कि वह पूर्ण वर्ग बन जाए? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)"},"2":{"en":"3"},"3":{"en":"9"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{16}\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(144p^2 - 72p = (12p)^2 - 2(12p)(3)\\)<br>Add \\(3^2\\) to complete the square: \\((12p - 3)^2\\)<br>Number \\(= \\boxed{9}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 9.</b>","hi":"\\(144p^2 - 72p = (12p)^2 - 2(12p)(3)\\)<br>वर्ग पूरा करने के लिए \\(3^2\\) जोड़िए: \\((12p - 3)^2\\)<br>संख्या \\(= \\boxed{9}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 9 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000072937","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Simplify the following expression: \\(\\frac{0.65 \\times 0.65 \\times 0.65 - 0.13 \\times 0.13 \\times 0.13}{0.65 \\times 0.65 + 0.65 \\times 0.13 + 0.13 \\times 0.13}\\). [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित व्यंजक को सरल कीजिए: \\(\\frac{0.65 \\times 0.65 \\times 0.65 - 0.13 \\times 0.13 \\times 0.13}{0.65 \\times 0.65 + 0.65 \\times 0.13 + 0.13 \\times 0.13}\\)। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.28"},"2":{"en":"0.52"},"3":{"en":"0.45"},"4":{"en":"0.76"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\) with \\(a = 0.65\\), \\(b = 0.13\\)<br>\\(= 0.65 - 0.13\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{0.52}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 0.52.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\), जहाँ \\(a = 0.65\\), \\(b = 0.13\\)<br>\\(= 0.65 - 0.13\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{0.52}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 0.52 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000072938","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"When a whole number x is added to 2026 and the same number x is subtracted from 2026, what is the sum of the two numbers so obtained? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"जब किसी पूर्ण संख्या x को 2026 में जोड़ा जाता है और वही संख्या x 2026 से घटाई जाती है, तो प्राप्त दोनों संख्याओं का योग क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1452"},"2":{"en":"4052"},"3":{"en":"3564"},"4":{"en":"2458"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The two numbers are \\((2026 + x)\\) and \\((2026 - x)\\)<br>Sum \\(= (2026 + x) + (2026 - x) = 2 \\times 2026\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{4052}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 4052.</b>","hi":"दोनों संख्याएँ \\((2026 + x)\\) और \\((2026 - x)\\) हैं<br>योग \\(= (2026 + x) + (2026 - x) = 2 \\times 2026\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{4052}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 4052 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000072939","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"Money is invested at simple interest for 3 years at a certain rate. If the rate were increased by 2%, the interest earned would increase by ₹540. Find the principal (sum of money). [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कोई धनराशि किसी दर पर 3 वर्षों के लिए साधारण ब्याज पर निवेश की जाती है। यदि दर 2% बढ़ा दी जाए, तो ब्याज ₹540 बढ़ जाता। मूलधन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹8,500"},"2":{"en":"₹9,000"},"3":{"en":"₹7,000"},"4":{"en":"₹8,000"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Extra interest \\(= \\frac{P \\times 2 \\times 3}{100} = 540\\)<br>\\(\\frac{6P}{100} = 540 \\Rightarrow P = \\frac{54000}{6}\\)<br>₹\\(P = \\boxed{9{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹9,000.</b>","hi":"अतिरिक्त ब्याज \\(= \\frac{P \\times 2 \\times 3}{100} = 540\\)<br>\\(\\frac{6P}{100} = 540 \\Rightarrow P = \\frac{54000}{6}\\)<br>₹\\(P = \\boxed{9{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹9,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000072940","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"An investment of ₹2,500 earns compound interest at 10% per annum. What will be the amount after 4 years? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"₹2,500 का निवेश 10% प्रति वर्ष चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज पर है। 4 वर्षों बाद मिश्रधन क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹3360.25"},"2":{"en":"₹3660.25"},"3":{"en":"₹3460.25"},"4":{"en":"₹3560.25"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(A = 2500(1.1)^4 = 2500 \\times 1.4641\\)<br>₹\\(= \\boxed{3660.25}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹3660.25.</b>","hi":"\\(A = 2500(1.1)^4 = 2500 \\times 1.4641\\)<br>₹\\(= \\boxed{3660.25}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹3660.25 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000072941","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A wheel of diameter 105 cm makes 40 revolutions. Find the distance covered (in meters). (Take π = 22/7) [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"105 cm व्यास वाला एक पहिया 40 चक्कर लगाता है। तय की गई दूरी (मीटर में) ज्ञात कीजिए। (π = 22/7 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"184 m"},"2":{"en":"208 m"},"3":{"en":"132 m"},"4":{"en":"216 m"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Circumference \\(= \\frac{22}{7} \\times 105 = 330\\) cm<br>Distance \\(= 40 \\times 330 = 13200\\) cm<br>\\(= \\boxed{132\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 132 m.</b>","hi":"परिधि \\(= \\frac{22}{7} \\times 105 = 330\\) cm<br>दूरी \\(= 40 \\times 330 = 13200\\) cm<br>\\(= \\boxed{132\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 132 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000072942","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In a circle with centre O, PQ is a chord, and T lies on the minor arc PQ. Tangents at points P and Q meet at point A. If ∠PTQ = 160°, then what is the measure of ∠PAQ? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"केंद्र O वाले एक वृत्त में PQ एक जीवा है और T लघु चाप PQ पर स्थित है। बिंदुओं P और Q पर स्पर्श रेखाएँ बिंदु A पर मिलती हैं। यदि ∠PTQ = 160° है, तो ∠PAQ का माप क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"40°"},"2":{"en":"70°"},"3":{"en":"100°"},"4":{"en":"140°"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"191\" height=\"242\" viewBox=\"0 0 191 242\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M39 107L95 26L152 107M43 110L47 106L42 102M147 110L144 106L149 102M39 107L95 77L152 107M86 82A10 10 0 0 0 104 82M88 36A12 12 0 0 0 102 36\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M95 147L39 107M95 147L152 107\"/><circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"147\" r=\"69\"/><circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"147\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"95\" y=\"163\">O</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"103\">P</text><text x=\"165\" y=\"103\">Q</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"23\">A</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"74\">T</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"103\" font-size=\"11\">160°</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"11\">?</text></g></svg><br>T on the minor arc gives the major-arc angle: \\(\\angle POQ = 2(180° - 160°) = 40°\\)<br>Radius is perpendicular to the tangent at the point of contact, so in quadrilateral OPAQ: \\(\\angle PAQ = 180° - \\angle POQ\\)<br>\\(\\angle PAQ = 180° - 40° = \\boxed{140°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 140°.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"191\" height=\"242\" viewBox=\"0 0 191 242\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M39 107L95 26L152 107M43 110L47 106L42 102M147 110L144 106L149 102M39 107L95 77L152 107M86 82A10 10 0 0 0 104 82M88 36A12 12 0 0 0 102 36\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M95 147L39 107M95 147L152 107\"/><circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"147\" r=\"69\"/><circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"147\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"95\" y=\"163\">O</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"103\">P</text><text x=\"165\" y=\"103\">Q</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"23\">A</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"74\">T</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"103\" font-size=\"11\">160°</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"11\">?</text></g></svg><br>T लघु चाप पर है, अतः दीर्घ चाप का कोण: \\(\\angle POQ = 2(180° - 160°) = 40°\\)<br>स्पर्श बिंदु पर त्रिज्या स्पर्श रेखा के लंबवत होती है, अतः चतुर्भुज OPAQ में: \\(\\angle PAQ = 180° - \\angle POQ\\)<br>\\(\\angle PAQ = 180° - 40° = \\boxed{140°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 140° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000072943","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If 20 sin θ + 21 cos θ = 29, find the value of sin θ. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 20 sin θ + 21 cos θ = 29 है, तो sin θ का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{21}{29}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{9}{29}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{20}{29}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{12}{29}\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Here \\(\\sqrt{20^2 + 21^2} = 29\\), so \\(\\sin\\theta = \\frac{20}{29}\\) and \\(\\cos\\theta = \\frac{21}{29}\\)<br>Check: \\(20\\left(\\frac{20}{29}\\right) + 21\\left(\\frac{21}{29}\\right) = \\frac{400 + 441}{29} = 29\\) ✓<br>\\(\\sin\\theta = \\boxed{\\frac{20}{29}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(\\frac{20}{29}\\).</b>","hi":"यहाँ \\(\\sqrt{20^2 + 21^2} = 29\\), अतः \\(\\sin\\theta = \\frac{20}{29}\\) और \\(\\cos\\theta = \\frac{21}{29}\\)<br>जाँच: \\(20\\left(\\frac{20}{29}\\right) + 21\\left(\\frac{21}{29}\\right) = \\frac{400 + 441}{29} = 29\\) ✓<br>\\(\\sin\\theta = \\boxed{\\frac{20}{29}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(\\frac{20}{29}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000072944","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x = \\sqrt{\\frac{10 + 3\\sqrt{11}}{10 - 3\\sqrt{11}}}\\), then what is the value of \\(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\)? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(x = \\sqrt{\\frac{10 + 3\\sqrt{11}}{10 - 3\\sqrt{11}}}\\) है, तो \\(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12"},"2":{"en":"14"},"3":{"en":"16"},"4":{"en":"20"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Rationalise: \\(\\frac{10 + 3\\sqrt{11}}{10 - 3\\sqrt{11}} = \\frac{(10 + 3\\sqrt{11})^2}{100 - 99} = (10 + 3\\sqrt{11})^2\\)<br>So \\(x = 10 + 3\\sqrt{11}\\) and \\(\\frac{1}{x} = 10 - 3\\sqrt{11}\\)<br>\\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = \\boxed{20}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 20.</b>","hi":"परिमेयकरण: \\(\\frac{10 + 3\\sqrt{11}}{10 - 3\\sqrt{11}} = \\frac{(10 + 3\\sqrt{11})^2}{100 - 99} = (10 + 3\\sqrt{11})^2\\)<br>अतः \\(x = 10 + 3\\sqrt{11}\\) और \\(\\frac{1}{x} = 10 - 3\\sqrt{11}\\)<br>\\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = \\boxed{20}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 20 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000072945","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"If △ABC ≅ △PQR and ∠ABC = (x + 60)°, ∠PQR = (85 − 4x)°, and ∠RPQ = (3x + 65)°, then what is the value of ∠ABC (in degrees)? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि △ABC ≅ △PQR और ∠ABC = (x + 60)°, ∠PQR = (85 − 4x)° तथा ∠RPQ = (3x + 65)° है, तो ∠ABC का मान (डिग्री में) क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45°"},"2":{"en":"65°"},"3":{"en":"25°"},"4":{"en":"55°"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"B corresponds to Q in △ABC ≅ △PQR, so \\(\\angle ABC = \\angle PQR\\)<br>\\(x + 60 = 85 - 4x \\Rightarrow 5x = 25 \\Rightarrow x = 5\\)<br>\\(\\angle ABC = 5 + 60 = \\boxed{65°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 65°.</b>","hi":"△ABC ≅ △PQR में B, Q के संगत है, अतः \\(\\angle ABC = \\angle PQR\\)<br>\\(x + 60 = 85 - 4x \\Rightarrow 5x = 25 \\Rightarrow x = 5\\)<br>\\(\\angle ABC = 5 + 60 = \\boxed{65°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 65° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000072946","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In △ABC, the internal bisector of ∠A meets BC at D. A point E lies on AC such that DE ∥ AB. If the length of AB = c, AC = b, and BC = a, determine the ratio of the area of △CDE to the area of △ABC in terms of b and c. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"△ABC में, ∠A का अंतः समद्विभाजक BC से D पर मिलता है। AC पर एक बिंदु E इस प्रकार है कि DE ∥ AB है। यदि AB = c, AC = b और BC = a है, तो △CDE और △ABC के क्षेत्रफलों का अनुपात b और c के पदों में ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\left(\\frac{c}{b + c}\\right)^2\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\left(\\frac{b}{b + c}\\right)^2\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{b}{b + c}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{c}{b + c}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"224\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 224\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M75 26L26 190L256 190ZM75 26L121 190M121 190L150 94M70 43A18 18 0 0 0 80 43M81 47A22 22 0 0 0 92 41\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"70\" y=\"17\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"201\">B</text><text x=\"271\" y=\"199\">C</text><text x=\"121\" y=\"201\">D</text><text x=\"157\" y=\"94\">E</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"108\">c</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"102\">b</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"11\">a</text><text x=\"139\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">DE ∥ AB</text></g></svg><br>By the angle-bisector theorem: \\(\\frac{BD}{DC} = \\frac{c}{b} \\Rightarrow \\frac{DC}{BC} = \\frac{b}{b + c}\\)<br>\\(DE \\parallel AB \\Rightarrow \\triangle CDE \\sim \\triangle CBA\\) with ratio \\(\\frac{DC}{BC}\\)<br>Area ratio \\(= \\left(\\frac{DC}{BC}\\right)^2 = \\boxed{\\left(\\frac{b}{b+c}\\right)^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\left(\\frac{b}{b + c}\\right)^2\\).</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"224\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 224\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M75 26L26 190L256 190ZM75 26L121 190M121 190L150 94M70 43A18 18 0 0 0 80 43M81 47A22 22 0 0 0 92 41\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"70\" y=\"17\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"201\">B</text><text x=\"271\" y=\"199\">C</text><text x=\"121\" y=\"201\">D</text><text x=\"157\" y=\"94\">E</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"108\">c</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"102\">b</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"11\">a</text><text x=\"139\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">DE ∥ AB</text></g></svg><br>कोण-समद्विभाजक प्रमेय से: \\(\\frac{BD}{DC} = \\frac{c}{b} \\Rightarrow \\frac{DC}{BC} = \\frac{b}{b + c}\\)<br>\\(DE \\parallel AB \\Rightarrow \\triangle CDE \\sim \\triangle CBA\\), अनुपात \\(\\frac{DC}{BC}\\)<br>क्षेत्रफल अनुपात \\(= \\left(\\frac{DC}{BC}\\right)^2 = \\boxed{\\left(\\frac{b}{b+c}\\right)^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\left(\\frac{b}{b + c}\\right)^2\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000072947","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two circles have radii of 10 cm and 4 cm, with the distance between their centers measuring 17 cm. Calculate the length of their transverse common tangent in centimeters. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो वृत्तों की त्रिज्याएँ 10 cm और 4 cm हैं, तथा उनके केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी 17 cm है। उनकी तिर्यक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा की लंबाई (cm में) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{83}\\) cm"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{93}\\) cm"},"3":{"en":"15 cm"},"4":{"en":"20 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"284\" height=\"202\" viewBox=\"0 0 284 202\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M157 50L210 127M101 101L163 58M228 101L204 118M158 62L161 67L166 63M209 115L205 110L200 113\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M101 101L228 101\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"101\" r=\"75\"/><circle cx=\"228\" cy=\"101\" r=\"30\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"101\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"228\" cy=\"101\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"98\" y=\"113\">A</text><text x=\"231\" y=\"113\">B</text><text x=\"165\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"11\">17</text><text x=\"161\" y=\"56\">P</text><text x=\"206\" y=\"129\">Q</text><text x=\"137\" y=\"91\">10</text><text x=\"212\" y=\"107\">4</text></g></svg><br>Transverse tangent \\(= \\sqrt{d^2 - (r_1 + r_2)^2}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{289 - 196} = \\sqrt{93}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\sqrt{93}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\sqrt{93}\\) cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"284\" height=\"202\" viewBox=\"0 0 284 202\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M157 50L210 127M101 101L163 58M228 101L204 118M158 62L161 67L166 63M209 115L205 110L200 113\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M101 101L228 101\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"101\" r=\"75\"/><circle cx=\"228\" cy=\"101\" r=\"30\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"101\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"228\" cy=\"101\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"98\" y=\"113\">A</text><text x=\"231\" y=\"113\">B</text><text x=\"165\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"11\">17</text><text x=\"161\" y=\"56\">P</text><text x=\"206\" y=\"129\">Q</text><text x=\"137\" y=\"91\">10</text><text x=\"212\" y=\"107\">4</text></g></svg><br>तिर्यक स्पर्श रेखा \\(= \\sqrt{d^2 - (r_1 + r_2)^2}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{289 - 196} = \\sqrt{93}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\sqrt{93}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\sqrt{93}\\) cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000072948","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If two angles of a triangle are \\(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\) radians and 45°, find the third angle in degrees. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि किसी त्रिभुज के दो कोण \\(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\) रेडियन और 45° हैं, तो तीसरा कोण डिग्री में ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"55°"},"2":{"en":"65°"},"3":{"en":"75°"},"4":{"en":"85°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{3} = 60°\\)<br>Third angle \\(= 180° - 60° - 45°\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{75°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 75°.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{3} = 60°\\)<br>तीसरा कोण \\(= 180° - 60° - 45°\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{75°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 75° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000072949","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sin A = \\frac{4}{5}\\) and \\(\\cos B = \\frac{5}{13}\\), where A and B are acute angles, then what is the value of sin A cos B? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sin A = \\frac{4}{5}\\) और \\(\\cos B = \\frac{5}{13}\\) हैं, जहाँ A और B न्यून कोण हैं, तो sin A cos B का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{20}{65}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(-\\frac{20}{65}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{16}{65}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{56}{65}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sin A\\cos B = \\frac{4}{5} \\times \\frac{5}{13}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{20}{65}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{20}{65}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\frac{20}{65}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\sin A\\cos B = \\frac{4}{5} \\times \\frac{5}{13}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{20}{65}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{20}{65}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\frac{20}{65}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000072950","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"In triangle PQR, right-angled at Q, if \\(\\tan P = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\), find sin R. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"त्रिभुज PQR में, Q पर समकोण है, यदि \\(\\tan P = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\) है, तो sin R ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan P = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\Rightarrow P = 30°\\), so \\(R = 90° - 30° = 60°\\)<br>\\(\\sin R = \\sin 60°\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan P = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\Rightarrow P = 30°\\), अतः \\(R = 90° - 30° = 60°\\)<br>\\(\\sin R = \\sin 60°\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000072951","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If a + b = 20, ab = 84, then find a⁴ + b⁴. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि a + b = 20, ab = 84 है, तो a⁴ + b⁴ ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"39012"},"2":{"en":"39112"},"3":{"en":"39332"},"4":{"en":"39712"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(a^2 + b^2 = 400 - 168 = 232\\)<br>\\(a^2b^2 = 84^2 = 7056\\)<br>\\(a^4 + b^4 = 232^2 - 2(7056) = 53824 - 14112\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{39712}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 39712.</b>","hi":"\\(a^2 + b^2 = 400 - 168 = 232\\)<br>\\(a^2b^2 = 84^2 = 7056\\)<br>\\(a^4 + b^4 = 232^2 - 2(7056) = 53824 - 14112\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{39712}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 39712 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000072952","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A circle has a radius of 13 cm. A tangent from an external point P has a length of 84 cm. The distance from the center of the circle to P is: [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक वृत्त की त्रिज्या 13 cm है। बाह्य बिंदु P से एक स्पर्श रेखा की लंबाई 84 cm है। वृत्त के केंद्र से P की दूरी है: [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"85 cm"},"2":{"en":"83 cm"},"3":{"en":"97 cm"},"4":{"en":"90 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"292\" height=\"116\" viewBox=\"0 0 292 116\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M266 58L63 26M58 58L63 26M62 33L69 34L70 27\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M58 58L266 58\"/><circle cx=\"58\" cy=\"58\" r=\"32\"/><circle cx=\"58\" cy=\"58\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"48\" y=\"62\">O</text><text x=\"276\" y=\"62\">P</text><text x=\"65\" y=\"17\">A</text><text x=\"51\" y=\"45\">13</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"33\">84</text><text x=\"178\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11\">d</text></g></svg><br>\\(OP = \\sqrt{r^2 + PT^2} = \\sqrt{169 + 7056}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{7225}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{85\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 85 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"292\" height=\"116\" viewBox=\"0 0 292 116\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M266 58L63 26M58 58L63 26M62 33L69 34L70 27\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M58 58L266 58\"/><circle cx=\"58\" cy=\"58\" r=\"32\"/><circle cx=\"58\" cy=\"58\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"48\" y=\"62\">O</text><text x=\"276\" y=\"62\">P</text><text x=\"65\" y=\"17\">A</text><text x=\"51\" y=\"45\">13</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"33\">84</text><text x=\"178\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11\">d</text></g></svg><br>\\(OP = \\sqrt{r^2 + PT^2} = \\sqrt{169 + 7056}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{7225}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{85\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 85 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000072953","section":"MATH","topic":"Average","question":{"en":"The average monthly expenditure of 36 families in a housing complex is ₹25,000. If 9 families, whose average expenditure is 40% higher than the overall initial average, move out, what is the percentage decrease in the overall average expenditure of the remaining families? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक आवास परिसर के 36 परिवारों का औसत मासिक व्यय ₹25,000 है। यदि 9 परिवार, जिनका औसत व्यय प्रारंभिक कुल औसत से 40% अधिक है, चले जाते हैं, तो शेष परिवारों के कुल औसत व्यय में कितने प्रतिशत कमी होगी? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8.00%"},"2":{"en":"10.00%"},"3":{"en":"12.50%"},"4":{"en":"13.33%"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Total \\(= 36 \\times 25{,}000 = 9{,}00{,}000\\)<br>9 families average \\(= 35{,}000\\) → total \\(3{,}15{,}000\\)<br>Remaining total \\(= 5{,}85{,}000\\) over 27 families → new average \\(= 21{,}666.67\\)<br>Decrease \\(= \\frac{25{,}000 - 21{,}666.67}{25{,}000} \\times 100 = \\boxed{13.33\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 13.33%.</b>","hi":"कुल \\(= 36 \\times 25{,}000 = 9{,}00{,}000\\)<br>9 परिवारों का औसत \\(= 35{,}000\\) → कुल \\(3{,}15{,}000\\)<br>शेष कुल \\(= 5{,}85{,}000\\), 27 परिवारों पर → नया औसत \\(= 21{,}666.67\\)<br>कमी \\(= \\frac{25{,}000 - 21{,}666.67}{25{,}000} \\times 100 = \\boxed{13.33\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 13.33% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000072954","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"A shopkeeper gains 25% after allowing a 20% discount on the marked price. By what percentage is the marked price higher than the cost price? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक दुकानदार अंकित मूल्य पर 20% छूट देकर 25% लाभ कमाता है। अंकित मूल्य क्रय मूल्य से कितने प्रतिशत अधिक है? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"42.5%"},"2":{"en":"59.66%"},"3":{"en":"56.25%"},"4":{"en":"62.2%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(0.8 \\times MP = 1.25 \\times CP \\Rightarrow MP = \\frac{1.25}{0.8}CP = 1.5625CP\\)<br>Mark-up \\(= 56.25\\%\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{56.25\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 56.25%.</b>","hi":"\\(0.8 \\times MP = 1.25 \\times CP \\Rightarrow MP = \\frac{1.25}{0.8}CP = 1.5625CP\\)<br>अंकन \\(= 56.25\\%\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{56.25\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 56.25% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000072955","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Simplify the following nested radical expression completely:<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4 + 2\\sqrt{3}}}\\) [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित बहुस्तरीय करणी व्यंजक को पूर्णतः सरल कीजिए:<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4 + 2\\sqrt{3}}}\\) [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{3} - 1\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{3} + 1\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1 - \\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(4 + 2\\sqrt{3} = (\\sqrt{3} + 1)^2\\), so \\(\\sqrt{4 + 2\\sqrt{3}} = \\sqrt{3} + 1\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3} + 1} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{3 - 1}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{2}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(4 + 2\\sqrt{3} = (\\sqrt{3} + 1)^2\\), अतः \\(\\sqrt{4 + 2\\sqrt{3}} = \\sqrt{3} + 1\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3} + 1} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{3 - 1}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000072956","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>The menstrual cycle, frequently distilled into reductive explanations within mainstream discourse, constitutes a complex, finely-tuned hormonal symphony that underpins female reproductive viability. Typically spanning around 28 days—though significant interindividual variability persists—the cycle is anatomically and biochemically demarcated into four sequential phases: menstruation, the follicular phase, ovulation, and the luteal phase.<br><br>Menstruation initiates with the systematic desquamation of the functional layer of the endometrium, an event precipitated by the precipitous decline in circulating levels of estrogen and progesterone following an unfertilized ovulatory event. Thereafter, during the follicular phase, anterior pituitary secretion of follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) catalyses the recruitment and maturation of ovarian follicles. A single dominant follicle subsequently prevails, secreting escalating quantities of estrogen to promote proliferative thickening of the endometrial lining in anticipation of potential zygote implantation.<br><br>Mid-cycle, ovulation ensues, triggered by an acute surge of luteinizing hormone (LH), culminating in the release of an oocyte into the fallopian tube — a transient but critical window of maximal fertility. In the absence of fertilization, the luteal phase commences: the residual follicular structure, now termed the corpus luteum, secretes progesterone to stabilize the endometrial architecture. Without embryonic implantation, corpus luteum regression ensues, hormonal concentrations diminish sharply, and the cyclical endometrial shedding recommences.<br><br>Despite the endogenous predictability of this sequence, the menstrual cycle exhibits considerable vulnerability to extrinsic perturbations — including psychosocial stressors, systemic illnesses, and environmental variables — underscoring the intricate interplay between endocrine function and broader homeostatic mechanisms.<br><br><br>Identify the correct transformation of the sentence.<br>“Menstruation initiates with the systematic desquamation of the functional layer of the endometrium.” Which option correctly transforms it into a passive voice without changing the meaning? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The functional layer of the endometrium is systematically desquamated, initiating menstruation."},"2":{"en":"Menstruation is initiating by the desquamation of the functional layer."},"3":{"en":"The systematic endometrium desquamates itself to initiate menstruation."},"4":{"en":"The menstruation systematically desquamates the functional layer of the endometrium."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: In passive voice, the object becomes the subject and the simple present takes “is/are + past participle”.</b><br>“The functional layer” becomes the subject, and “initiates with the systematic desquamation” is expressed as “is systematically desquamated.”<br>Option 2 uses the incorrect form “is initiating”; option 3 changes the agent and meaning; option 4 remains active and adds an unnecessary article.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The functional layer of the endometrium is systematically desquamated, initiating menstruation.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000072957","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>The menstrual cycle, frequently distilled into reductive explanations within mainstream discourse, constitutes a complex, finely-tuned hormonal symphony that underpins female reproductive viability. Typically spanning around 28 days—though significant interindividual variability persists—the cycle is anatomically and biochemically demarcated into four sequential phases: menstruation, the follicular phase, ovulation, and the luteal phase.<br><br>Menstruation initiates with the systematic desquamation of the functional layer of the endometrium, an event precipitated by the precipitous decline in circulating levels of estrogen and progesterone following an unfertilized ovulatory event. Thereafter, during the follicular phase, anterior pituitary secretion of follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) catalyses the recruitment and maturation of ovarian follicles. A single dominant follicle subsequently prevails, secreting escalating quantities of estrogen to promote proliferative thickening of the endometrial lining in anticipation of potential zygote implantation.<br><br>Mid-cycle, ovulation ensues, triggered by an acute surge of luteinizing hormone (LH), culminating in the release of an oocyte into the fallopian tube — a transient but critical window of maximal fertility. In the absence of fertilization, the luteal phase commences: the residual follicular structure, now termed the corpus luteum, secretes progesterone to stabilize the endometrial architecture. Without embryonic implantation, corpus luteum regression ensues, hormonal concentrations diminish sharply, and the cyclical endometrial shedding recommences.<br><br>Despite the endogenous predictability of this sequence, the menstrual cycle exhibits considerable vulnerability to extrinsic perturbations — including psychosocial stressors, systemic illnesses, and environmental variables — underscoring the intricate interplay between endocrine function and broader homeostatic mechanisms.<br><br><br>According to the passage, what is the primary function of the corpus luteum during the luteal phase? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To trigger menstruation by lowering progesterone."},"2":{"en":"To secrete hormones that maintain endometrial integrity."},"3":{"en":"To stimulate another round of follicle maturation."},"4":{"en":"To dissolve immediately after ovulation."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Corpus luteum: progesterone secretion and endometrial support.</b><br><i>“The residual follicular structure, now termed the corpus luteum, secretes progesterone to stabilize the endometrial architecture.”</i><br>Thus, it maintains the endometrial lining during the luteal phase.<br>Lowering progesterone leads to shedding, not its primary function; follicle maturation belongs to the follicular phase; dissolution follows only when implantation does not occur.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): To secrete hormones that maintain endometrial integrity.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000072958","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>The menstrual cycle, frequently distilled into reductive explanations within mainstream discourse, constitutes a complex, finely-tuned hormonal symphony that underpins female reproductive viability. Typically spanning around 28 days—though significant interindividual variability persists—the cycle is anatomically and biochemically demarcated into four sequential phases: menstruation, the follicular phase, ovulation, and the luteal phase.<br><br>Menstruation initiates with the systematic desquamation of the functional layer of the endometrium, an event precipitated by the precipitous decline in circulating levels of estrogen and progesterone following an unfertilized ovulatory event. Thereafter, during the follicular phase, anterior pituitary secretion of follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) catalyses the recruitment and maturation of ovarian follicles. A single dominant follicle subsequently prevails, secreting escalating quantities of estrogen to promote proliferative thickening of the endometrial lining in anticipation of potential zygote implantation.<br><br>Mid-cycle, ovulation ensues, triggered by an acute surge of luteinizing hormone (LH), culminating in the release of an oocyte into the fallopian tube — a transient but critical window of maximal fertility. In the absence of fertilization, the luteal phase commences: the residual follicular structure, now termed the corpus luteum, secretes progesterone to stabilize the endometrial architecture. Without embryonic implantation, corpus luteum regression ensues, hormonal concentrations diminish sharply, and the cyclical endometrial shedding recommences.<br><br>Despite the endogenous predictability of this sequence, the menstrual cycle exhibits considerable vulnerability to extrinsic perturbations — including psychosocial stressors, systemic illnesses, and environmental variables — underscoring the intricate interplay between endocrine function and broader homeostatic mechanisms.<br><br><br>Choose the correct form of the verb for the blank:<br>“Despite the endogenous predictability of this sequence, the menstrual cycle ___ considerable vulnerability to extrinsic perturbations.” [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"exhibits"},"2":{"en":"exhibit"},"3":{"en":"exhibiting"},"4":{"en":"exhibited"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: A singular subject takes a singular present-tense verb.</b><br>The subject “the menstrual cycle” is singular, so “exhibits” is correct.<br>Completed sentence: “The menstrual cycle <b>exhibits</b> considerable vulnerability to extrinsic perturbations.”<br>“Exhibit” is plural, “exhibiting” cannot serve as the finite verb here, and “exhibited” changes the general present fact to the past.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): exhibits.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000072959","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>The menstrual cycle, frequently distilled into reductive explanations within mainstream discourse, constitutes a complex, finely-tuned hormonal symphony that underpins female reproductive viability. Typically spanning around 28 days—though significant interindividual variability persists—the cycle is anatomically and biochemically demarcated into four sequential phases: menstruation, the follicular phase, ovulation, and the luteal phase.<br><br>Menstruation initiates with the systematic desquamation of the functional layer of the endometrium, an event precipitated by the precipitous decline in circulating levels of estrogen and progesterone following an unfertilized ovulatory event. Thereafter, during the follicular phase, anterior pituitary secretion of follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) catalyses the recruitment and maturation of ovarian follicles. A single dominant follicle subsequently prevails, secreting escalating quantities of estrogen to promote proliferative thickening of the endometrial lining in anticipation of potential zygote implantation.<br><br>Mid-cycle, ovulation ensues, triggered by an acute surge of luteinizing hormone (LH), culminating in the release of an oocyte into the fallopian tube — a transient but critical window of maximal fertility. In the absence of fertilization, the luteal phase commences: the residual follicular structure, now termed the corpus luteum, secretes progesterone to stabilize the endometrial architecture. Without embryonic implantation, corpus luteum regression ensues, hormonal concentrations diminish sharply, and the cyclical endometrial shedding recommences.<br><br>Despite the endogenous predictability of this sequence, the menstrual cycle exhibits considerable vulnerability to extrinsic perturbations — including psychosocial stressors, systemic illnesses, and environmental variables — underscoring the intricate interplay between endocrine function and broader homeostatic mechanisms.<br><br><br>What does “desquamation” most closely mean in the context of the passage? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Thickening of the uterine lining"},"2":{"en":"Shedding of the surface layer"},"3":{"en":"Hormone secretion"},"4":{"en":"Cell multiplication"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Desquamation (सतही परत का झड़ना) = shedding of a surface layer of cells.</b><br><i>“Menstruation initiates with the systematic desquamation of the functional layer of the endometrium.”</i><br>The menstrual context makes “shedding of the surface layer” the precise meaning.<br>Thickening is proliferation; hormone secretion is a glandular action; cell multiplication is proliferation, not shedding.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Shedding of the surface layer.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000072960","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>The menstrual cycle, frequently distilled into reductive explanations within mainstream discourse, constitutes a complex, finely-tuned hormonal symphony that underpins female reproductive viability. Typically spanning around 28 days—though significant interindividual variability persists—the cycle is anatomically and biochemically demarcated into four sequential phases: menstruation, the follicular phase, ovulation, and the luteal phase.<br><br>Menstruation initiates with the systematic desquamation of the functional layer of the endometrium, an event precipitated by the precipitous decline in circulating levels of estrogen and progesterone following an unfertilized ovulatory event. Thereafter, during the follicular phase, anterior pituitary secretion of follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) catalyses the recruitment and maturation of ovarian follicles. A single dominant follicle subsequently prevails, secreting escalating quantities of estrogen to promote proliferative thickening of the endometrial lining in anticipation of potential zygote implantation.<br><br>Mid-cycle, ovulation ensues, triggered by an acute surge of luteinizing hormone (LH), culminating in the release of an oocyte into the fallopian tube — a transient but critical window of maximal fertility. In the absence of fertilization, the luteal phase commences: the residual follicular structure, now termed the corpus luteum, secretes progesterone to stabilize the endometrial architecture. Without embryonic implantation, corpus luteum regression ensues, hormonal concentrations diminish sharply, and the cyclical endometrial shedding recommences.<br><br>Despite the endogenous predictability of this sequence, the menstrual cycle exhibits considerable vulnerability to extrinsic perturbations — including psychosocial stressors, systemic illnesses, and environmental variables — underscoring the intricate interplay between endocrine function and broader homeostatic mechanisms.<br><br><br>What is the closest synonym for the word “precipitous” as used in the passage? [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Abrupt"},"2":{"en":"Gradual"},"3":{"en":"Moderate"},"4":{"en":"Predictable"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Precipitous (अचानक, तीव्र) = sudden and very steep or rapid.</b><br><b>Abrupt (अचानक)</b> = happening suddenly ✔<br><b>Gradual (क्रमिक)</b> = occurring slowly by degrees<br><b>Moderate (मध्यम)</b> = average in intensity or amount<br><b>Predictable (पूर्वानुमानित)</b> = able to be foreseen<br>More synonyms: sudden, sharp, rapid.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Abrupt.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000072961","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Identify the correct active voice transformation of the following sentence.<br>The vase had been shattered by the cat. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The cat had shattered the vase."},"2":{"en":"The cat shatters the vase."},"3":{"en":"The vase had shattered the cat."},"4":{"en":"The cat shattered the vase."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Had been + past participle” changes to “had + past participle” in active voice.</b><br>The agent “the cat” becomes the subject and “the vase” becomes the object: “The cat <b>had shattered</b> the vase.”<br>Option 2 changes the tense to simple present; option 3 reverses subject and object illogically; option 4 changes past perfect to simple past.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The cat had shattered the vase.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000072962","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word. <b>PANACEA</b> [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Remedy"},"2":{"en":"Solution"},"3":{"en":"Universal cure"},"4":{"en":"Treatment"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Panacea (रामबाण) = a remedy believed to cure all diseases or solve all problems.</b><br><b>Remedy (उपचार)</b> = a treatment for a particular problem<br><b>Solution (समाधान)</b> = an answer to a problem<br><b>Universal cure (सर्वरोगहर औषधि)</b> = a cure for everything ✔<br><b>Treatment (उपचार)</b> = medical care given for illness<br>More synonyms: cure-all, elixir, sovereign remedy.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Universal cure.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000072963","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word. <b>CONVICTION</b> [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Doubt"},"2":{"en":"Certainty"},"3":{"en":"Confusion"},"4":{"en":"Hesitation"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Conviction (दृढ़ विश्वास) = a firmly held belief or certainty.</b><br><b>Doubt (संदेह)</b> = uncertainty or lack of belief<br><b>Certainty (निश्चितता)</b> = firm assurance ✔<br><b>Confusion (भ्रम)</b> = lack of clarity<br><b>Hesitation (हिचकिचाहट)</b> = reluctance caused by uncertainty<br>More synonyms: assurance, belief, certitude.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Certainty.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000072964","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Tacit</b> [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Expressed"},"2":{"en":"Implied"},"3":{"en":"Informed"},"4":{"en":"Understood"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Tacit (अकथित, मौन) = understood or implied without being stated.</b><br><b>Expressed (अभिव्यक्त)</b> = stated openly in words ✔<br><b>Implied (निहित)</b> = suggested but not directly stated<br><b>Informed (सूचित)</b> = having or giving information<br><b>Understood (समझा गया)</b> = grasped mentally<br>More antonyms: explicit, stated, declared.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Expressed.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000072965","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Choose the sentence containing the homonym of the underlined word:<br>She had a bright <u>pupil</u> in her class. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The pupil of his eye was dilated."},"2":{"en":"The pupil was late for school."},"3":{"en":"The new pupil performed well."},"4":{"en":"The pupil solved the problem quickly."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Homonym: a word with the same spelling and pronunciation but a different meaning.</b><br>In the given sentence, “pupil” means a student (छात्र).<br>In option 1, “pupil” means the dark central opening of the eye (आँख की पुतली), so it is the homonym.<br>Options 2, 3 and 4 all use “pupil” in the original sense of a student.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The pupil of his eye was dilated.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000072966","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the below given passive voice sentence into active voice.<br>“The new policy was announced by the minister during the press conference”. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The minister announces the new policy during the press conference"},"2":{"en":"The minister announced the new policy during the press conference"},"3":{"en":"The minister is announcing the new policy during the press conference"},"4":{"en":"The minister had announced the new policy during the press conference"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Was/were + past participle” changes to the simple past in active voice.</b><br>The agent “the minister” becomes the subject, giving “The minister <b>announced</b> the new policy during the press conference.”<br>Option 1 uses simple present; option 3 uses present continuous; option 4 incorrectly changes the tense to past perfect.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The minister announced the new policy during the press conference.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000072967","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Four parts of a sentence are given below in a jumbled order. When arranged correctly, they form a complete and meaningful sentence. While multiple combinations may appear grammatically correct, choose the one that best conveys the intended meaning as per the given options.<br>A) in Tamil Nadu<br>B) was inaugurated<br>C) a new desalination plant<br>D) by the Prime Minister [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"B-D-C-A"},"2":{"en":"D-C-B-A"},"3":{"en":"C-B-D-A"},"4":{"en":"C-D-B-A"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: C-B-D-A</b><br>C supplies the subject, “a new desalination plant.”<br>B provides the passive verb “was inaugurated,” and D names the agent, “by the Prime Minister.”<br>A ends with the location “in Tamil Nadu”: “A new desalination plant was inaugurated by the Prime Minister in Tamil Nadu.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): C-B-D-A.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000072968","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Four parts of a sentence are given below in a jumbled order. When arranged correctly, they form a complete and meaningful sentence. While multiple combinations may appear grammatically correct, choose the one that best conveys the intended meaning as per the given options.<br>A) due to better crop prices<br>B) rural consumption<br>C) in recent years<br>D) has seen steady growth [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"C-B-D-A"},"2":{"en":"B-D-C-A"},"3":{"en":"A-D-B-C"},"4":{"en":"D-A-B-C"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: B-D-C-A</b><br>B gives the subject, “rural consumption,” followed by D, “has seen steady growth.”<br>C supplies the time frame “in recent years.”<br>A gives the reason “due to better crop prices,” completing a natural sentence.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): B-D-C-A.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000072969","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Identify the misspelt word: [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Magnanimous"},"2":{"en":"Gregarious"},"3":{"en":"Perserverance"},"4":{"en":"Meticulous"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Perseverance (दृढ़ता) = persistence in doing something despite difficulty.</b><br><b>Perserverance</b> is misspelt: the correct sequence is “per-se-ver-ance,” not “per-ser-ver-ance.”<br><b>Magnanimous (उदार)</b> = generous or forgiving; spelling correct.<br><b>Gregarious (मिलनसार)</b> = sociable; spelling correct.<br><b>Meticulous (सूक्ष्मता से कार्य करने वाला)</b> = very careful and precise; spelling correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Perserverance.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000072970","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the correct degree of comparison:<br>This project is far ___ than the previous one. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Easy"},"2":{"en":"easier"},"3":{"en":"easiest"},"4":{"en":"more easiest"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Use the comparative adjective before “than.”</b><br>The comparative of “easy” is “easier,” and “far” intensifies the comparison.<br>Completed sentence: “This project is far <b>easier</b> than the previous one.”<br>“Easy” is positive degree, “easiest” is superlative, and “more easiest” is a double comparative error.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): easier.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000072971","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“Put the cart before the horse” [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Prioritize tasks logically"},"2":{"en":"Reverse the proper order"},"3":{"en":"Show urgency"},"4":{"en":"Delegate responsibility"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Put the cart before the horse (काम का उल्टा क्रम रखना)</b><br>It means to do things in the wrong order or reverse their natural sequence.<br>Example: “Buying furniture before renting a house is putting the cart before the horse.”<br>Prioritizing logically is the opposite; showing urgency concerns speed; delegating responsibility means assigning work to another person.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Reverse the proper order.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000072972","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“Break new ground” [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Create a mess"},"2":{"en":"Innovate or pioneer"},"3":{"en":"Destroy something"},"4":{"en":"Start agriculture"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Break new ground (नया क्षेत्र खोलना, नवप्रवर्तन करना)</b><br>It means to make a discovery or do something innovative for the first time.<br>Example: “The research team broke new ground in cancer treatment.”<br>Creating a mess and destroying something are unrelated; starting agriculture is only a literal interpretation.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Innovate or pioneer.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000072973","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Choose the correctly spelt word that best completes the sentence meaningfully.<br>His ___ car blocked the main road for hours, causing a major traffic jam. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"stationary"},"2":{"en":"stationery"},"3":{"en":"statuary"},"4":{"en":"statutory"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Stationary (स्थिर) = not moving.</b><br>A blocked car is stationary, so the sentence needs “stationary.”<br><b>Stationery (लेखन-सामग्री)</b> = writing materials<br><b>Statuary (मूर्तिकला)</b> = statues collectively<br><b>Statutory (वैधानिक)</b> = required or authorized by law<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): stationary.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000072974","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the most appropriate option:<br>He was reprimanded not for the error itself, but for his evasion ___ responsibility thereafter. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"of"},"2":{"en":"for"},"3":{"en":"to"},"4":{"en":"towards"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The noun “evasion” is followed by the preposition “of.”</b><br>“Evasion of responsibility” means avoiding responsibility (जिम्मेदारी से बचना).<br>Completed sentence: “He was reprimanded not for the error itself, but for his evasion <b>of</b> responsibility thereafter.”<br>“For,” “to” and “towards” do not form the standard noun–preposition combination here.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): of.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000072975","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the most appropriate option:<br>The analyst's conclusion, while mathematically valid, was marred by a glaring ___ of contextual variables. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"abstinence"},"2":{"en":"integration"},"3":{"en":"omission"},"4":{"en":"alignment"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Omission (चूक, लोप) = the act of leaving something out.</b><br>A glaring omission of contextual variables means an obvious failure to include relevant factors.<br><b>Abstinence (संयम)</b> = restraint from an activity<br><b>Integration (एकीकरण)</b> = combining parts into a whole<br><b>Alignment (संरेखण)</b> = arrangement in agreement or a straight line<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): omission.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000072976","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitution for:<br>A person who engages in espionage. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Diplomat"},"2":{"en":"Spy"},"3":{"en":"Proprietor"},"4":{"en":"Investigator"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Spy (जासूस) = a person who secretly collects information, especially for a government.</b><br><b>Diplomat (राजनयिक)</b> = an official representing a country abroad<br><b>Proprietor (स्वामी)</b> = the owner of a business or property<br><b>Investigator (अन्वेषक)</b> = a person who examines facts systematically<br>Engaging in espionage is specifically the work of a spy.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Spy.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000072977","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the underlined part of the sentence:<br>She walked into the room <u>with silent steps</u>. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"with silenced"},"2":{"en":"insilence"},"3":{"en":"silently"},"4":{"en":"silence"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: An adverb modifies the verb “walked.”</b><br>“Silently” describes how she walked and replaces the wordy phrase “with silent steps.”<br>Correct sentence: “She walked into the room <b>silently</b>.”<br>“With silenced” is incomplete, “insilence” is not a valid written form, and the noun “silence” cannot directly modify “walked.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): silently.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000072978","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful passage.<br>1. Next, the patient is given a mild sedative.<br>2. First, the doctor checks vital signs.<br>3. After the procedure, the patient is monitored for side effects.<br>4. Then, the injection is administered. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-1-4-3"},"2":{"en":"2-3-1-4"},"3":{"en":"1-2-4-3"},"4":{"en":"1-2-3-4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-1-4-3</b><br>Sentence 2 opens with “First,” when the doctor checks vital signs.<br>Sentence 1 follows with “Next,” and sentence 4 continues with “Then,” when the injection is administered.<br>Sentence 3 closes the sequence with monitoring “after the procedure.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2-1-4-3.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000072979","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful passage<br>1. A new cohort of civil officers is inducted through lateral recruitment streams.<br>2. Training schedules are personalized via role-specific benchmarks.<br>3. Induction records are submitted for background standardization.<br>4. Cross-department placements are finalized. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4-3-2-1"},"2":{"en":"3-2-1-4"},"3":{"en":"2-1-4-3"},"4":{"en":"1-3-2-4"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 1-3-2-4</b><br>Sentence 1 introduces the induction of a new cohort.<br>Sentence 3 follows with submission of induction records, then sentence 2 describes personalized training.<br>Sentence 4 gives the final stage: cross-department placements.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 1-3-2-4.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000072980","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word:<br>She caught the <b>train</b> just before it departed. [SSC CGL 07/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He had to train hard for the marathon."},"2":{"en":"The train was unusually delayed."},"3":{"en":"They boarded the overnight train."},"4":{"en":"The steam train whistled loudly."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Homonym: the same word form used with a different meaning.</b><br>In the given sentence, “train” is a railway vehicle (रेलगाड़ी).<br>In option 1, “train” is a verb meaning to practise or prepare (अभ्यास करना), so it is the homonym.<br>Options 2, 3 and 4 retain the railway-vehicle meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): He had to train hard for the marathon.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};